" Documentation License då och då. Sådana nya versioner kommer att vara "
"likadana i andemening som den nuvarande versionen, men kan skilja i detalj "
"för att behandla nya problem eller angelägenheter. Se <ulink "
"url=\"https://www.gnu.org/copyleft/\">https://www.gnu.org/copyleft/</ulink>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"Each version of the License is given a distinguishing version number. If the"
" Document specifies that a particular numbered version of this License "
"<quote>or any later version</quote> applies to it, you have the option of "
"following the terms and conditions either of that specified version or of "
"any later version that has been published (not as a draft) by the Free "
"Software Foundation. If the Document does not specify a version number of "
"this License, you may choose any version ever published (not as a draft) by "
"the Free Software Foundation."
msgstr ""
"Varje version av licensen ges ett unikt versionsnummer. Om dokumentet "
"stadgar att en specifik numrerad version av denna licens <quote>eller valfri"
" senare version</quote> gäller för det, så äger du rätten att följa "
"villkoren enligt antingen den angivna versionen eller vilken senare version "
"som helst som publicerats (inte som utkast) av Free Software Foundation. Om "
"dokumentet inte anger en version av denna licens, har du rätt att välja "
"vilken version som helst som publicerats (inte som utkast) av Free Software "
"Foundation."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid "ADDENDUM: How to use this License for your documents"
msgstr "TILLÄGG: Hur du använder denna licens för dina dokument"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
#. from gnome:reviewed/gtk-doc/master
msgid ""
"To use this License in a document you have written, include a copy of the "
"License in the document and put the following copyright and license notices "
"just after the title page:"
msgstr ""
"För att använda GNU Free Documentation License för ett dokument du har "
"skrivit, inkludera en kopia av licensen [det engelska originalet] i "
"dokumentet och placera följande copyrightklausul omedelbart efter "
"titelsidan:"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"Copyright (c) YEAR YOUR NAME. Permission is granted to copy, distribute "
"and/or modify this document under the terms of the GNU Free Documentation "
"License, Version 1.2 or any later version published by the Free Software "
"Foundation; with no Invariant Sections, no Front-Cover Texts, and no Back-"
"Cover Texts. A copy of the license is included in the section entitled "
"<quote>GNU Free Documentation License</quote>."
msgstr ""
"Copyright (c) ÅR DITT NAMN. Permission is granted to copy, distribute and/or"
" modify this document under the terms of the GNU Free Documentation License,"
" Version 1.2 or any later version published by the Free Software Foundation;"
" with no Invariant Sections, no Front-Cover Texts, and no Back-Cover Texts. "
"A copy of the license is included in the section entitled <quote>GNU Free "
"Documentation License</quote>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"If you have Invariant Sections, Front-Cover Texts and Back-Cover Texts, "
"replace the <quote>with...Texts.</quote> line with this:"
msgstr ""
"Om du har oföränderliga avsnitt, framsidestexter och baksidestexter, ersätt "
"raden <quote>with...Texts.</quote> med detta:"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"with the Invariant Sections being LIST THEIR TITLES, with the Front-Cover "
"Texts being LIST, and with the Back-Cover Texts being LIST."
msgstr ""
"with the Invariant Sections being LISTA DERAS TITLAR, with the Front-Cover "
"Texts being LISTA, and with the Back-Cover Texts being LISTA."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"If you have Invariant Sections without Cover Texts, or some other "
"combination of the three, merge those two alternatives to suit the "
"situation."
msgstr ""
"Om du har oföränderliga avsnitt utan omslagstexter, eller någon annan "
"kombination av de tre, slå samman dessa två alternativ för att passa "
"situationen."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"If your document contains nontrivial examples of program code, we recommend "
"releasing these examples in parallel under your choice of free software "
"license, such as the GNU General Public License, to permit their use in free"
" software."
msgstr ""
"Om ditt dokument innehåller icke-triviala exempel med programkod, så "
"rekommenderar vi att du släpper dessa exempel parallellt under en, av dig "
"vald, fri programvarulicens, som till exempel GNU General Public License, "
"för att möjliggöra deras användning i fri programvara."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"@@image: 'images/contribute/xml-tags.png'; "
"md5=6b7e682efd4abdaf4694086de617e0a8"
msgstr ""
"@@image: 'images/contribute/xml-tags.png'; "
"md5=6b7e682efd4abdaf4694086de617e0a8"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid "How to Contribute"
msgstr "Hur du bidrar"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid "How to contribute"
msgstr "Hur du bidrar"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid "Welcome to the GIMP-Help team!"
msgstr "Välkommen till GIMP-hjälpgruppen!"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"This tutorial is intended for writing documentation. If you want to "
"<emphasis>translate</emphasis> the documentation or the user interface, "
"please go to \"https://l10n.gnome.org/teams/xx\" where \"xx\" is your "
"language code: ISO 639-1 language codes can be found at <ulink "
"url=\"https://www.loc.gov/standards/iso639-2/php/code_list.php\"/>."
msgstr ""
"Denna handledning är avsedd för att skriva dokumentation. Om du vill "
"<emphasis>översätta</emphasis> dokumentationen eller användargränssnittet, "
"gå till ”https://l10n.gnome.org/teams/xx” där ”xx” är din språkkod: ISO "
"639-1-språkkoder kan hittas på <ulink "
"url=\"https://www.loc.gov/standards/iso639-2/php/code_list.php\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr "Förutsättningar"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid "Join Discourse"
msgstr "Gå med i Discourse"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"You can join <ulink url=\"https://discourse.gnome.org/\">Gnome's Discourse "
"server</ulink> and subscribe to the <ulink "
"url=\"https://discourse.gnome.org/tag/gimp\">gimp</ulink> and <ulink "
"url=\"https://discourse.gnome.org/tag/documentation\">documentation</ulink> "
"tags. Please, feel free to ask questions. If you do, remember to set the "
"relevant tags, or we may not see the message."
msgstr ""
"Du kan gå med i <ulink url=\"https://discourse.gnome.org/\">GNOMEs "
"Discourse-server</ulink> och prenumerera på taggarna <ulink "
"url=\"https://discourse.gnome.org/tag/gimp\">gimp</ulink> och <ulink "
"url=\"https://discourse.gnome.org/tag/documentation\">documentation</ulink>."
" Välkommen att ställa frågor. Om du gör det, kom ihåg att sätta de relevanta"
" taggarna, annars ser vi kanske inte meddelandet."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid "Create a Local Working Copy of Code"
msgstr "Skapa en lokal fungerande kopia av koden"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"The GIMP help Manual is lodged in a central repository at "
"https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gimp-help. Creating a local copy of this "
"repository to work on makes sure that everyone can work on his own without "
"fuzzing around into works of other contributors."
msgstr ""
"GIMP-hjälpmanualen finns i ett centralt arkiv på "
"https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gimp-help. Att skapa en lokal kopia av detta "
"arkiv för att arbeta på säkerställer att alla kan arbeta på egen hand utan "
"att behöva blanda in arbetet från andra bidragsgivare."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"As a newbie, you will access the git repository anonymously (without an "
"account). Open a terminal and type: <emphasis> git clone "
"https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gimp-help.git </emphasis>."
msgstr ""
"Som en nybörjare kommer du att vilja komma åt git-arkivet anonymt (utan ett "
"konto). Öppna en terminal och skriv: <emphasis>git clone "
"https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gimp-help.git</emphasis>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"If you have a GNOME account, the command is: <emphasis> git clone "
"git@gitlab.gnome.org:GNOME/gimp-help.git </emphasis>."
msgstr ""
"Om du har ett GNOME-konto är kommandot: <emphasis> git clone "
"git@gitlab.gnome.org:GNOME/gimp-help.git </emphasis>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"This will create a <quote>gimp-help</quote> folder in your current "
"directory. Be patient! That's a big download: about 700 MB."
msgstr ""
"Detta kommer att skapa en mapp <quote>gimp-help</quote> i din aktuella "
"katalog. Var tålmodig! Det är en stor hämtning: cirka 700 MB."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid "Installing your sandbox"
msgstr "Installera din sandlåda"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"After downloading your local copy, run: <emphasis>cd gimp-help</emphasis> "
"then <emphasis>./autogen.sh --without-gimp ALL_LINGUAS=\"en xx\"</emphasis>."
msgstr ""
"Efter att du hämtat ner din lokala kopia, kör: <emphasis>cd gimp-"
"help</emphasis> och sedan <emphasis>./autogen.sh --without-gimp "
"ALL_LINGUAS=\"en xx\"</emphasis>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"When running ./autogen.sh, you can notice some not found packages, for "
"example <quote>checking for dblatex... no</quote>. Most of them are related "
"to PDF files and you have to install them before running ./autogen.sh again "
"if you want to create PDF files."
msgstr ""
"När du kör ./autogen.sh kanske du ser att några paket saknas, till exempel "
"<quote>checking for dblatex... no</quote>. Merparten av dem är relaterade "
"till PDF-filer och du måste installera dem innan du kör ./autogen.sh igen om"
" du vill skapa PDF-filer."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid "The gimp-help folder"
msgstr "Mappen gimp-help"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"The GIMP User Manual is maintained in the xml files of the "
"<quote>src</quote> folder. You will use these xml files to work on."
msgstr ""
"GIMPs användarmanual underhålls i xml-filerna i <quote>src</quote>-mappen. "
"Du kommer att arbeta med dessa xml-filer."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid "The language is English (USA)."
msgstr "Språket är engelska (USA)."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid "English-US language."
msgstr "Engelska (USA)."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"Indent with 2 spaces (the <keycap>Tab</keycap> key must move pointer by two "
"spaces)."
msgstr ""
"Indentera med 2 blanksteg (tangenten <keycap>Tabb</keycap> måste flytta "
"markören två blanksteg)."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"Replace tabs with spaces (for compatibility with all text editors and web "
"browsers)."
msgstr ""
"Ersätt tabbar med blanksteg (för kompatibilitet med alla textredigerare och "
"webbläsare)."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid "80 characters per line."
msgstr "80 tecken per rad."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid "Automatic spell checking with English (USA) for default language."
msgstr "Automatisk stavningskontroll med engelska (USA) som standardspråk."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"To edit XML files, use your preferred text editor (this guide's author "
"prefers the free editor Kate). You must set the editor for: <placeholder-1/>"
msgstr ""
"Använd din favorittextredigerare för att redigera XML-filer (guidens "
"författare föredrar den fria redigeraren Kate). Du måste ställa in "
"redigeraren på: <placeholder-1/>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"Source files are written in the XML language according to the DocBook DTD. "
"DocBook specifications can be found at <ulink "
"url=\"https://tdg.docbook.org/tdg/4.5/docbook.html\"/>."
msgstr ""
"Källfiler skrivs i XML-språket enligt DocBook-DTD:n. DocBook-specifikationer"
" hittas på <ulink url=\"https://tdg.docbook.org/tdg/4.5/docbook.html\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"Don't be afraid. We don't use all these items and you will learn XML "
"progressively reading existing XML files. For new files, please use the "
"templates you can find in the gimp-help/docs/templates folder."
msgstr ""
"Var inte rädd. Vi använder inte alla dessa objekt och du kommer att lära dig"
" XML stegvis genom att läsa befintliga XML-filer. För nya filer, använd "
"mallarna som du hittar i mappen gimp-help/docs/templates."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"If you write a new file, you must add it in the src/gimp.xml file, or in the"
" XML file that calls it (for example, the src/menus/edit.xml file calls "
"undo.xml, redo.xml, fade.xml, and so on)."
msgstr ""
"Om du skriver en ny fil, måste du lägga till den i filen src/gimp.xml, eller"
" i XML-filen som anropar den (till exempel så anropar filen "
"src/menus/edit.xml filerna undo.xml, redo.xml, fade.xml och så vidare)."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"For a single file, you can use the following command line: <command>xmllint "
"--noout --nonet --valid your-file.xml</command>. This command displays "
"nothing if your file is OK. When an error is found it will show a message "
"indicating the kind of error and where in your file it was encountered."
msgstr ""
"På kommandoraden kan du för en enstaka fil använda: <command>xmllint --noout"
" --nonet --valid din-fil.xml</command>. Detta kommando visar ingenting om "
"din fil är OK. Om ett fel hittas kommer det visa ett meddelande som "
"indikerar feltypen och var i filen det påträffades."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"This command can be used for quickly checking an xml file. It can miss or "
"may not find some errors. In case of external references to other files it "
"also may show incorrect error messages, because this command only checks a "
"single file."
msgstr ""
"Detta kommando kan användas för att snabbt kontrollera en xml-fil. Det kan "
"missa eller inte hitta vissa fel. I fallet med externa referenser till andra"
" filer kan det också visa felaktiga felmeddelanden, för kommandot "
"kontrollerar bara en enda fil."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"(The Kate editor has an option (a plug-in) to validate the active xml file.)"
msgstr ""
"(Textredigeraren Kate har ett alternativ (en insticksmodul) för att validera"
" den aktiva xml-filen.)"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"When you want to check multiple files or the whole gimp-help repository you "
"should run <command>make validate-en</command>. You should get a <quote>No "
"error</quote> message."
msgstr ""
"När du vill kontrollera flera filer eller hela gimp-help-arkivet kör du "
"<command>make validate-en</command>. Du bör erhålla meddelandet <quote>Inget"
" fel</quote>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"If not, a list of validity errors is displayed with line numbers referring "
"to the en.xml log file that you can find in the /log folder."
msgstr ""
"Annars kommer en lista över valideringsfel att visas med radnummer som "
"refererar till loggfilen en.xml som du hittar i mappen /log."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"Open this en.xml file in a text editor, use the <quote>jump to line</quote> "
"command of your editor (the Kate editor command is "
"<keycombo><keycap>Ctrl</keycap><keycap>G</keycap></keycombo>), and enter the"
" line number to jump to the concerned line in the en.xml file. There, you "
"will find the error."
msgstr ""
"Öppna denna fil, en.xml, i en textredigerare och använd textredigerarens "
"kommando för att <quote>hoppa till rad</quote> (kommandot för detta i "
"textredigeraren Kate är "
"<keycombo><keycap>Ctrl</keycap><keycap>G</keycap></keycombo>) och mata in "
"radnumret för att hoppa till den berörda raden i filen en.xml. Där kommer du"
" att hitta felet."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"If you have worked on several XML files, look above in the en.xml file to "
"find (in the <quote>xml:base</quote> field of the <quote>id</quote> tag), in"
" which xml file the error is."
msgstr ""
"Om du har arbetat på flera XML-filer, se ovan i filen en.xml för att hitta "
"(i fältet <quote>xml:base</quote> i taggen <quote>id</quote>) i vilken xml-"
"fil felet finns."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"Fix the error. Don't forget to save the file and run <command>make validate-"
"en</command> again."
msgstr ""
"Fixa felet. Glöm inte att spara filen och kör <command>make validate-"
"en</command> igen."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"A common mistake is editing the en.xml log file instead of the XML file."
msgstr ""
"Ett vanligt misstag är att redigera loggfilen en.xml i stället för XML-"
"filen."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"When you have finished writing, you should validate your work: "
"<placeholder-1/>"
msgstr "När du skrivit klart bör du validera ditt arbete: <placeholder-1/>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"reduce screenshot area as much as possible cropping the window manager "
"borders and disabling the help button (you can do it in the preference "
"dialog),"
msgstr ""
"reducera skärmbildsområdet så mycket som möjligt och beskär "
"fönsterhanterarens ramar och inaktivera hjälpknappen (du kan göra detta i "
"inställningsdialogen),"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"set the image mode to indexed 255 colors "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Image</guimenu><guisubmenu>Mode</guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Indexed</guimenuitem></menuchoice>"
msgstr ""
"ställ in bildläget på 255 indexerade färger "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Bild</guimenu><guisubmenu>Läge</guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Indexerad</guimenuitem></menuchoice>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"This is not necessary for icons and if your image has only few colors. In "
"these cases, indexed images are bigger than non-indexed."
msgstr ""
"Detta är inte nödvändigt för ikoner och om din bild endast har ett fåtal "
"färger. I dessa fall kan indexerade bilder vara större än icke-indexerade."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"set print resolution to 144 ppi (not for small images like icons). You can "
"do this easily with GIMP from "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Image</guimenu><guisubmenu>Print "
"Size…</guisubmenu></menuchoice>"
msgstr ""
"ställ in utskriftsupplösningen till 144 ppi (inte för små bilder såsom "
"ikoner). Du kan lätt göra detta i GIMP från menyn "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Bild</guimenu><guisubmenu>Utskriftsstorlek…</guisubmenu></menuchoice>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid "Export images in the PNG format."
msgstr "Exportera bilder i PNG-formatet."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"You also have to manage screenshots. Here are some hints for making good "
"screenshots: <placeholder-1/>"
msgstr ""
"Du måste också hantera skärmbilder. Här kommer några tips för att göra bra "
"skärmbilder: <placeholder-1/>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"Don't include English text in images. Translators can't translate it and "
"many users don't like that. Use XML captions instead, or provide a .xcf file"
" in the <menuchoice><guimenu>Docs</guimenu><guisubmenu>xcf "
"images</guisubmenu></menuchoice> folder, indicating it by a comment in the "
"XML file: <markup>&lt;!--TO TRANSLATORS: Corresponding .xcf file is in "
"https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gimp-help/tree/master/docs/xcf%20images "
"--&gt;</markup>"
msgstr ""
"Inkludera inte engelsk text i bilder. Översättare kan inte översätta den och"
" många användare tycker inte om detta. Använd XML-bildtexter i stället, "
"eller tillhandahåll en .xcf-fil i mappen "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>docs</guimenu><guisubmenu>xcf "
"images</guisubmenu></menuchoice> och indikera detta med en kommentar i XML-"
"filen: <markup>&lt;!--TO TRANSLATORS: Corresponding .xcf file is in "
"https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gimp-help/tree/master/docs/xcf%20images "
"--&gt;</markup>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"Icons for GIMP are in <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr/share/gimp/&gimp.api.version;/icons/</filename>. "
"GTK icons are in <filename class=\"directory\">/usr/share/icons/</filename>."
msgstr ""
"Ikoner för GIMP finns i <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr/share/gimp/&gimp.api.version;/icons/</filename>. "
"GTK-ikoner finns i <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr/share/icons/</filename>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"To include an icon in the text: <markup> &lt;guiicon&gt; "
"&lt;inlinemediaobject&gt; &lt;imageobject&gt; &lt;imagedata fileref=\"path-"
"to-icon\"/&gt; &lt;/imageobject&gt; &lt;/inlinemediaobject&gt; "
"&lt;/guiicon&gt; </markup>"
msgstr ""
"För att inkludera en ikon i texten: <markup> &lt;guiicon&gt; "
"&lt;inlinemediaobject&gt; &lt;imageobject&gt; &lt;imagedata "
"fileref=\"sökväg-till-ikon\"/&gt; &lt;/imageobject&gt; "
"&lt;/inlinemediaobject&gt; &lt;/guiicon&gt; </markup>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"<command>make check-image-resolutions-en</command>: gives the references of "
"images whose resolution is not 144 ppi."
msgstr ""
"<command>make check-image-resolutions-en</command>: ger referenser till "
"bilder vars upplösning inte är 144 ppi."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"<command>make check-images-en</command>: give references of missing or "
"orphaned images."
msgstr ""
"<command>make check-images-en</command>: ger referenser till bilder som "
"saknas eller är övergivna."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"<command>mogrify units PixelsPerTrack -density 144x144 *.png</command> to "
"set the print resolution of all PNG images."
msgstr ""
"<command>mogrify units PixelsPerTrack -density 144x144 *.png</command> för "
"att skriva ut upplösningen på alla PNG-bilder."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid "Three commands to manage your images: <placeholder-1/>"
msgstr "Tre kommandon för att hantera dina bilder: <placeholder-1/>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid "Create HTML Files"
msgstr "Skapa HTML-filer"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"Once XML files have been validated, run <command>make html-en</command>. "
"Creating HTML files is important to have an idea about what users will see. "
"You will probably notice some improvements to be made on your XML file."
msgstr ""
"När XML-filerna har validerats, kör <command>make html-en</command>. Att "
"skapa HTML-filer är viktigt för att ha en uppfattning om vad användarna "
"kommer att se. Du kommer förmodligen upptäcka några förbättringar som kan "
"göras i din XML-fil."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"You can make an HTML draft (when the folder xml/en has been created during "
"validation) for a single source xml file, by running, for instance, the "
"command <command>make preview-xml/en/path-to-file.xml</command>. This "
"creates draft.html file in the html folder."
msgstr ""
"Du kan skapa ett HTML-utkast (när mappen xml/en har skapats under "
"valideringen) för en enstaka xml-källfil genom att till exempel köra "
"kommandot <command>make preview-xml/en/sökväg-till-fil.xml</command>. Detta "
"skapar en fil draft.html i html-mappen."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"You can also use <acronym>yelp</acronym> and run <command>yelp file:///your-"
"file.xml</command>."
msgstr ""
"Du kan också använda <acronym>yelp</acronym> och köra <command> yelp "
"file:///din-fil.xml</command>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid "Sending your files"
msgstr "Att skicka dina filer"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid "When your files are ready:"
msgstr "När dina filer är klara:"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid "You don't have a GNOME account"
msgstr "Du har inte ett GNOME-konto"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"if you don't have a GNOME account, you must find a correspondent who accepts"
" to \"push\" files for you; that will not be difficult if you send a message"
" to the list. Either you send your xml files and the attached images in a "
"compressed file, (in a tree reproducing that of the src and images folders "
"if you send several files to make your correspondent's task easier), or you "
"send a \"patch\" that you have to create."
msgstr ""
"om du inte har ett GNOME-konto måste du hitta en person som accepterar att "
"”push:a” filerna åt dig; det kommer inte att vara svårt om du skickar ett "
"meddelande till listan. Skicka antingen dina xml-filer och bifoga bilderna i"
" en komprimerad fil, (i ett träd som reproducerar det i src- och images-"
"mapparna om du skickar flera filer för att göra mottagarens uppgift enklare)"
" eller om du skickar en ”patch” (programfix) som du måste skapa."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"Before creating a patch, you have to get all your xml files and images in "
"the index. Being in the gimp-help folder, do <command>git status</command>. "
"If you have files in the Untracked files section, run <command>git add "
"-A</command>."
msgstr ""
"Innan du skapar en programfix måste du få in alla dina xml-filer och bilder "
"i indexet. Om du är i mappen gimp-help, kör <command>git status</command>. "
"Om du har filer i avsnittet Ospårade filer, kör <command>git add "
"-A</command>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"Then run <command>git diff --full-index --binary origin &gt; name-of-the-"
"patch</command> to create the patch."
msgstr ""
"Kör sedan <command>git diff --full-index --binary origin &gt; namnet-på-"
"programfixen</command> för att skapa programfixen."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid "You have a GNOME account"
msgstr "Du har ett GNOME-konto"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid ""
"All being well, you know how to manage Git. There are many tutorials for "
"that on the Web."
msgstr ""
"I bästa fall vet du hur du hanterar Git. Det finns många guider för det på "
"nätet."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gimp-help — GIMP User Manual/master
msgid "A common workflow is:"
msgstr "Ett vanligt arbetsflöde är:"

