"”status” är standardåtgärden, vilket betyder att ”nmcli gen” anropar ”nmcli gen status”\n"
"\n"

#. from gnome:reviewed/NetworkManager/main
msgid ""
"Usage: nmcli general hostname { ARGUMENTS | help }\n"
"\n"
"ARGUMENTS := [<hostname>]\n"
"\n"
"Get or change persistent system hostname.\n"
"With no arguments, this prints currently configured hostname. When you pass\n"
"a hostname, NetworkManager will set it as the new persistent system hostname.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"Användning: nmcli general hostname { ARGUMENTS | help }\n"
"\n"
"ARGUMENTS := [<värdnamn>]\n"
"\n"
"Hämta eller ändra permanent systemvärdnamn.\n"
"Om inga argument anges skrivs det aktuella konfigurerade värdnamnet ut. Om\n"
"du anger ett värdnamn anger Nätverkshanteraren det som nytt permanent systemvärdnamn.\n"
"\n"

#. from gnome:reviewed/NetworkManager/main
msgid ""
"Usage: nmcli general permissions { help }\n"
"\n"
"Show caller permissions for authenticated operations.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"Användning: nmcli general permissions { help }\n"
"\n"
"Visar anropsrättigheter för autentiserade åtgärder.\n"
"\n"

#. from gnome:reviewed/NetworkManager/main
msgid ""
"Usage: nmcli general reload { ARGUMENTS | help }\n"
"\n"
"ARGUMENTS := [<flag>[,<flag>...]]\n"
"\n"
"Reload NetworkManager's configuration and perform certain updates, like\n"
"flushing caches or rewriting external state to disk. This is similar to\n"
"sending SIGHUP to NetworkManager but it allows for more fine-grained\n"
"control over what to reload through the flags argument. It also allows\n"
"non-root access via PolicyKit and contrary to signals it is synchronous.\n"
"\n"
"Available flags are:\n"
"\n"
"  'conf'        Reload the NetworkManager.conf configuration from\n"
"                disk. Note that this does not include connections, which\n"
"                can be reloaded through 'nmcli connection reload' instead.\n"
"\n"
"  'dns-rc'      Update DNS configuration, which usually involves writing\n"
"                /etc/resolv.conf anew. This is equivalent to sending the\n"
"                SIGUSR1 signal to the NetworkManager process.\n"
"\n"
"  'dns-full'    Restart the DNS plugin. This is for example useful when\n"
"                using dnsmasq plugin, which uses additional configuration\n"
"                in /etc/NetworkManager/dnsmasq.d. If you edit those files,\n"
"                you can restart the DNS plugin. This action shortly\n"
"                interrupts name resolution.\n"
"\n"
"With no flags, everything that is supported is reloaded, which is\n"
"identical to sending a SIGHUP.\n"
msgstr ""
"Användning: nmcli general reload { ARGUMENTS | help }\n"
"\n"
"ARGUMENTS := [<flagga>[,<flagga>…]]\n"
"\n"
"Ladda om Nätverkshanterarens konfiguration och utför vissa uppdateringar, till\n"
"exempel rensa cacheminnen eller skriva om externt tillstånd till disk. Detta\n"
"liknar att skicka SIGHUP till NetworkManager, men ger mer detaljerad\n"
"kontroll över vad som laddas om via flaggargumentet. Det ger också\n"
"icke-root-åtkomst via PolicyKit och är, till skillnad från signaler, synkront.\n"
"\n"
"Tillgängliga flaggor är:\n"
"\n"
"  'conf'        Ladda om NetworkManager.conf-konfigurationen från\n"
"                disk. Observera att anslutningar inte ingår utan i stället\n"
"                kan laddas om med 'nmcli connection reload'.\n"
"\n"
"  'dns-rc'      Uppdatera DNS-konfigurationen, vilket vanligen innebär\n"
"                att /etc/resolv.conf skrivs på nytt. Detta motsvarar att\n"
"                skicka SIGUSR1 till NetworkManager-processen.\n"
"\n"
"  'dns-full'    Starta om DNS-insticksmodulen. Det är till exempel användbart\n"
"                när dnsmasq-insticksmodulen används med ytterligare konfiguration i\n"
"                /etc/NetworkManager/dnsmasq.d. Om du redigerar filerna kan\n"
"                DNS-insticksmodulen startas om. Åtgärden avbryter kortvarigt\n"
"                namnupplösningen.\n"
"\n"
"Utan flaggor laddas allt som stöds om; det motsvarar att skicka en\n"
"SIGHUP.\n"

#. from gnome:reviewed/NetworkManager/main
msgid ""
"Usage: nmcli general logging { ARGUMENTS | help }\n"
"\n"
"ARGUMENTS := [level <log level>] [domains <log domains>]\n"
"\n"
