#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Immediately above the grid of cells is the data entry area as shown in <xref"
" linkend=\"worksheet-data-1\"/>."
msgstr ""
"Ovanför cellrutnätet finns inmatningsfältet, som visas i <xref "
"linkend=\"worksheet-data-1\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"<imageobject> <imagedata fileref=\"figures/worksheet-data-1.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>An image of the data "
"entry area.</phrase> </textobject>"
msgstr ""
"<imageobject> <imagedata fileref=\"figures/worksheet-data-1.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>En bild av "
"inmatningsfältet.</phrase> </textobject>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"This is a small area, which contains a current cell indicator, a "
"<guibutton>cancel</guibutton> button, a <guibutton>confirm</guibutton> "
"button, an <guibutton>entry</guibutton> button, and an entry area for "
"detailed editing of the cell contents. These elements are explained "
"individually below."
msgstr ""
"Det här lilla området innehåller en indikator för aktuell cell, knapparna "
"<guibutton>Avbryt</guibutton>, <guibutton>Bekräfta</guibutton> och "
"<guibutton>Inmatning</guibutton> samt ett fält där du kan redigera "
"cellinnehållet i detalj. Varje del beskrivs nedan."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"On the far left of the Data Entry area is the current cell indicator area. "
"This area is shown in <xref linkend=\"worksheet-data-2\"/>"
msgstr ""
"Längst till vänster i inmatningsfältet finns indikatorn för aktuell cell, "
"som visas i <xref linkend=\"worksheet-data-2\"/>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"<imageobject> <imagedata fileref=\"figures/worksheet-data-2.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>An image of the current"
" cell indicator.</phrase> </textobject>"
msgstr ""
"<imageobject> <imagedata fileref=\"figures/worksheet-data-2.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>En bild av indikatorn "
"för aktuell cell.</phrase> </textobject>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The cell indicator will show the address for the cell at the top left of the"
" selected region. This address is listed in the standard column:row "
"notation. The alphabetic part indicates the column of this top leftmost cell"
" and the numeric part indicates the row of this top left cell. For instance,"
" the cell which is over three columns and down two rows is designated:"
msgstr ""
"Cellindikatorn visar adressen till cellen längst upp till vänster i det "
"markerade området. Adressen anges med standardformatet kolumn:rad. Bokstaven"
" anger kolumnen för den cellen och siffran anger raden. Cellen tre kolumner "
"åt höger och två rader ned anges till exempel så här:"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"While a region is being selected, the current cell indicator will change to "
"show the size of the region which is being selected. This information is "
"presented in a row number by column number format. For instance, this "
"designation: <_:blockquote-1/> would indicate a selection area 15 rows high "
"by 6 columns wide. Once the mouse is released at the end of the selection, "
"the current cell indicator goes back to giving the address of the single top"
" leftmost cell."
msgstr ""
"När du markerar ett område ändras cellindikatorn så att den visar områdets "
"storlek. Storleken anges som antal rader gånger antal kolumner. Beteckningen"
" <_:blockquote-1/> anger till exempel ett markerat område som är 15 rader "
"högt och 6 kolumner brett. När du släpper musknappen återgår indikatorn till"
" att visa adressen för den enskilda cellen längst upp till vänster."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The Cancel button <guibutton> <inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/worksheet-data-4.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> "
"<textobject> <phrase>An image of the cancel button.</phrase> </textobject> "
"</inlinemediaobject> </guibutton> can be used to cancel the current edit and"
" to restore the cell contents to the previous state. If a user decides in "
"the middle of an edit that the data being entered into a cell is not what "
"they want, the user can push this cancel button to cancel the current data "
"and return the cell to the state it was at before."
msgstr ""
"Med knappen Avbryt <guibutton> <inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/worksheet-data-4.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> "
"<textobject> <phrase>En bild av avbrytknappen.</phrase> </textobject> "
"</inlinemediaobject> </guibutton> avbryter du redigeringen och återställer "
"cellinnehållet till föregående tillstånd. Om du under redigeringen märker "
"att du håller på att skriva in fel data kan du klicka på knappen för att "
"avbryta inmatningen och återställa cellen."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The most common use of this button is when overwriting the contents of a "
"cell with new data. If the user decided to revert the change before "
"confirming it, the cancel button is the answer. Note that this button works "
"just like typing the escape key on the keyboard."
msgstr ""
"Knappen används oftast när du ersätter en cells innehåll med nya data. Om du"
" ångrar dig innan du har bekräftat ändringen klickar du på Avbryt. Knappen "
"fungerar på samma sätt som att trycka på Escape."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The confirm button <guibutton> <inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/worksheet-data-3.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> "
"<textobject> <phrase>An image of the enter button.</phrase> </textobject> "
"</inlinemediaobject> </guibutton>. can be used to finish the edit of a cell "
"and enter the edit into the workbook. Note that this button works in the "
"same way as the enter key."
msgstr ""
"Med bekräftelseknappen <guibutton> <inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> "
"<imagedata fileref=\"figures/worksheet-data-3.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> "
"</imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>En bild av Enter-knappen.</phrase> "
"</textobject> </inlinemediaobject> </guibutton> slutför du redigeringen av "
"en cell och för in ändringen i arbetsboken. Knappen fungerar på samma sätt "
"som Enter-tangenten."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The equals button <guibutton> <inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/button-equals.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> "
"<textobject> <phrase>An image of the equals button.</phrase> </textobject> "
"</inlinemediaobject> </guibutton> can be used to start a formula in the "
"currently selected cell. If a user wanted to make cell D10 equal to cell B4,"
" the user could simply click on cell D10, click this equals button, click on"
" cell B4 and type the enter key. Note that this button works the same way as"
" the equals key."
msgstr ""
"Med likhetsteckenknappen <guibutton> <inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> "
"<imagedata fileref=\"figures/button-equals.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> "
"</imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>En bild av "
"likhetsteckenknappen.</phrase> </textobject> </inlinemediaobject> "
"</guibutton> kan du påbörja en formel i den markerade cellen. Om cell D10 "
"ska få samma värde som cell B4 klickar du först på D10, sedan på "
"likhetsteckenknappen och därefter på B4. Tryck sedan på Enter. Knappen "
"fungerar på samma sätt som likhetsteckentangenten."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Most of the work done on a spreadsheet is done to the main Cell area, the "
"large grid like part of the worksheet. This is where all the formulas and "
"data are entered, and is the center of activity for the spreadsheet."
msgstr ""
"Det mesta arbetet i ett kalkylprogram sker i cellområdet, den stora "
"rutnätsdelen av kalkylbladet. Här skriver du in formler och data; det är "
"kalkylbladets huvudsakliga arbetsyta."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"<xref linkend=\"cell-grid.png\"/> shows the cell grid area, the column and "
"row headers on the top and left, the scrollbars on the right and bottom and "
"the tab list at the very bottom."
msgstr ""
"<xref linkend=\"cell-grid.png\"/> visar cellrutnätet, kolumn- och "
"radrubrikerna överst och till vänster, rullningslisterna till höger och "
"längst ned samt bladflikarna längst ned."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The figure has a few and shows that cell B3 as being selected. In this "
"figure, the columns and rows have been resized and therefore look uneven."
msgstr ""
"Figuren visar bland annat att cell B3 är markerad. Kolumnerna och raderna "
"har ändrats i storlek och är därför olika breda respektive höga."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Each cell in this area is delimited by a light grey line by default. The "
"current selection is indicated by a rectangular box with a little box on the"
" lower right, this case cell J12. The view in this figure shows the middle "
"portion of a worksheet which is evident in two ways. Firstly, the column and"
" row headers do not start at column A and row 1. Secondly, the scroll thumbs"
" are not at the top and left. The thumbs are the boxes within the scroll "
"bars that are used to scroll. Note also that cell D19 has a comment within "
"it which is shown by the little red triangle at the top right corner."
msgstr ""
"Som standard avgränsas cellerna av tunna grå linjer. Den aktuella "
"markeringen visas som en rektangel med en liten ruta nere till höger; här är"
" cell J12 markerad. Figuren visar mitten av ett kalkylblad, vilket framgår "
"av att kolumn- och radrubrikerna inte börjar vid kolumn A och rad 1, och att"
" rullningslisternas handtag inte står längst upp eller till vänster. "
"Handtagen är rutorna som du drar i för att rulla. Lägg också märke till "
"kommentaren i cell D19, som markeras med en liten röd triangel i det övre "
"högra hörnet."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The size of a cell is determined by the width of the column and height of "
"the row that the cell is in. The columns and rows can be resized by acting "
"on the header relevant to the cell. The user must move the mouse pointer to "
"the edge of the header which is either to the right or below the cell. With "
"the mouse pointer in this position, the pointer will change to a set of "
"opposite pointing arrows. The user must then drag this edge away from the "
"top left corner. This takes a little practice."
msgstr ""
"Cellens storlek bestäms av bredden på kolumnen och höjden på raden den "
"ligger i. Du kan ändra storlek på kolumner och rader genom att dra i "
"respektive rubrik. Placera pekaren vid rubrikens kant, till höger om "
"kolumnen eller under raden. Pekaren ändras då till två motriktade pilar. Dra"
" kanten bort från det övre vänstra hörnet. Det kan krävas lite övning."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The cell area is the core of Gnumeric. Therefore the manual explains the use"
" of cells in much greater detail in a separate section. Interested users "
"should read <xref linkend=\"chapter-data\"/>."
msgstr ""
"Cellområdet är kärnan i Gnumeric. Därför behandlar manualen celler mer "
"ingående i ett eget avsnitt. Läs <xref linkend=\"chapter-data\"/> om du vill"
" veta mer."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The sheet is bordered by column headers on the top and row headers to the "
"left. Columns are labeled alphabetically running horizontally across the top"
" of the sheet as shown in <xref linkend=\"worksheet-cols-1\"/>. "
"<_:figure-1/> Rows are labeled along the left side of the worksheet. Each "
"label is a different integer increasing downward. This is shown in <xref "
"linkend=\"worksheet-rows-1\"/>. <_:figure-2/>"
msgstr ""
"Kalkylbladet har kolumnrubriker överst och radrubriker till vänster. "
"Kolumnerna betecknas med bokstäver i vågrät riktning, som i <xref "
"linkend=\"worksheet-cols-1\"/>. <_:figure-1/> Raderna betecknas med heltal "
"längs kalkylbladets vänstra sida, i stigande ordning nedåt. Det visas i "
"<xref linkend=\"worksheet-rows-1\"/>. <_:figure-2/>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The cell grid area's scrollbars work like other scrollbars. In this case "
"they let the user work on a worksheet which is much bigger than what could "
"be shown at any given moment."
msgstr ""
"Rullningslisterna för cellrutnätet fungerar som andra rullningslister. De "
"gör att du kan arbeta med kalkylblad som är större än det område som ryms på"
" skärmen."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"At the bottom of <xref linkend=\"cell-grid.png\"/>, Gnumeric has a tabbed "
"sheet indicator. This is the boxes with the labels \"Guppies\", \"Turtles\","
" \"Mermaids\", \"seahorses\" and so on. In workbooks where there are more "
"than one sheet, extra tabs are used to indicate how many sheets are there, "
"and also allows the user to move to another sheet by clicking the proper "
"tab. Each tab is a link to a separate worksheet within Gnumeric. In this "
"figure, the \"Turtles\" tab has been selected. Gnumeric shows this by making"
" the \"Turtles\" since the tab is a little bigger and making it overlap the "
"two neighbouring tabs."
msgstr ""
"Längst ned i <xref linkend=\"cell-grid.png\"/> visar Gnumeric bladflikarna, "
"här märkta ”Guppyer”, ”Sköldpaddor”, ”Sjöjungfrur”, ”sjöhästar” och så "
"vidare. Om en arbetsbok innehåller flera blad visas en flik för varje blad. "
"Klicka på en flik för att byta till det bladet. Varje flik leder till ett "
"separat kalkylblad i Gnumeric. I figuren är fliken ”Sköldpaddor” markerad. "
"Den är något större och överlappar de två intilliggande flikarna."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"On the far right, the two arrows indicate that there are more sheets in the "
"workbook and more tabs for those sheets. Unfortunately, there is not enough "
"space to show them all so Gnumeric displays these arrows. If all the sheets "
"are visible, these arrows will not be displayed. These arrows can be used to"
" scroll the tabs and bring tabs that were hidden into view. This may be a "
"little difficult to understand and work with but becomes easier quickly."
msgstr ""
"De två pilarna längst till höger visar att arbetsboken innehåller fler blad "
"och flikar än vad som får plats. Pilarna visas inte om alla blad redan syns."
" Använd dem för att rulla bland flikarna och visa de dolda flikarna. Det kan"
" kännas ovant först, men blir snart lättare."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The section at the very bottom of the worksheet view is the information area"
" as is shown in <xref linkend=\"info-area.png\"/>. <_:figure-1/> The "
"information area displays information depending on what is happening in "
"Gnumeric."
msgstr ""
"Längst ned i kalkylbladsvyn finns informationsfältet, som visas i <xref "
"linkend=\"info-area.png\"/>. <_:figure-1/> Fältet visar information om det "
"som för tillfället händer i Gnumeric."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The leftmost portion of the information display area, the part which reads: "
"\"Sort the selected cells\" is a hint explaining what a menu does. In this "
"case, the Data menu was opened and the pointer is hovering above the "
"\"sort\" menu entry. Gnumeric is responding by giving a quick explanation of"
" what that menu entry does."
msgstr ""
"Den vänstra delen av informationsfältet, där det står: ”Sortera de markerade"
" cellerna”, visar ett tips om vad ett menyobjekt gör. I det här fallet är "
"menyn Data öppen och pekaren ligger över menyobjektet ”Sortera”. Gnumeric "
"visar då en kort förklaring av kommandot."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Whenever Gnumeric opens or saves a file, the file status indicator appears "
"with a progress bar which grows as Gnumeric progresses. In <xref "
"linkend=\"info-area.png\"/>, Gnumeric was just over halfway done opening a "
"file."
msgstr ""
"När Gnumeric öppnar eller sparar en fil visas en förloppsindikator som fylls"
" i takt med att arbetet fortskrider. I <xref linkend=\"info-area.png\"/> har"
" Gnumeric kommit lite mer än halvvägs genom att öppna en fil."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"In the bottom right hand corner, is an info area that shows some constantly "
"calculated values. The default set is to show the Sum of all the currently "
"selected cells."
msgstr ""
"Längst ned till höger finns ett informationsfält som visar värden som "
"beräknas löpande. Som standard visas summan av alla markerade celler."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"There is a right click option that includes a few more options. This can "
"include Sum, Min, Max, Average, Count."
msgstr ""
"Via snabbmenyn kan du välja fler beräkningar, till exempel Summa, Min, Max, "
"Medelvärde och Antal."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The shape of the mouse pointer (the pointer which is movable by the mouse) "
"changes in different contexts. This indicates that different functionality "
"is available and that mouse clicks will have different results. The "
"different mouse pointers and the actions they indicate are discussed below."
msgstr ""
"Muspekaren ändrar utseende beroende på sammanhang. Det visar att olika "
"funktioner är tillgängliga och att musklick kan ge olika resultat. Nedan "
"beskrivs de olika pekarna och vad de används till."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/pointer_left.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> "
"<textobject> <phrase>An arrow pointing to the upper left.</phrase> "
"</textobject> </inlinemediaobject> The left pointing arrow pointer:"
msgstr ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/pointer_left.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> "
"<textobject> <phrase>En pil som pekar snett uppåt åt vänster.</phrase> "
"</textobject> </inlinemediaobject> Den vänsterpekande pilpekaren:"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The left hand pointing arrow pointer is the standard pointer used for most "
"of the interaction with <application>Gnumeric</application>. This pointer is"
" used to select menus and menu entries, toolbar buttons, columns or rows, "
"the scrolling `thumbs' and various other elements."
msgstr ""
"Den vänsterpekande pilpekaren är standardpekaren och används vid de flesta "
"interaktioner med <application>Gnumeric</application>. Med den väljer du "
"menyer och menyobjekt, verktygsfältsknappar, kolumner och rader, "
"rullningslisternas handtag och andra objekt."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/pointer_cross_wide.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> "
"<textobject> <phrase>A wide white cross with black shading.</phrase> "
"</textobject> </inlinemediaobject> The cell selection pointer:"
msgstr ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/pointer_cross_wide.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> "
"<textobject> <phrase>Ett brett vitt kors med svart skuggning.</phrase> "
"</textobject> </inlinemediaobject> Cellmarkeringspekaren:"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"This pointer appears over the cell grid area and can be used to select cells"
" for editing."
msgstr ""
"Den här pekaren visas över cellrutnätet och används för att markera celler "
"som ska redigeras."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/pointer_text_edit.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> "
"<textobject> <phrase>A vertical bar limited at each end by short horizontal "
"stubs.</phrase> </textobject> </inlinemediaobject> The text editing pointer:"
msgstr ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/pointer_text_edit.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> "
"<textobject> <phrase>Ett lodrätt streck med korta tvärstreck i båda "
"ändarna.</phrase> </textobject> </inlinemediaobject> Textredigeringspekaren:"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The text editing pointer is used to indicate the location in the text where "
"new edits will appear. This cursor can be used to change the scale of the "
"zoom, to change the name and size of the font currently used or to edit the "
"cell contents in the cell entry area (the white area to the right of the "
"equals (=) sign."
msgstr ""
"Textredigeringspekaren visar var ny text kommer att infogas. Den kan "
"användas för att ändra zoomnivån, byta namn på eller storlek för det "
"aktuella teckensnittet och redigera cellinnehållet i inmatningsfältet (det "
"vita området till höger om likhetstecknet (=))."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/pointer_cross_hair.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> "
"<textobject> <phrase>A thin cross pointer</phrase> </textobject> "
"</inlinemediaobject> The cross hair pointer:"
msgstr ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/pointer_cross_hair.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> "
"<textobject> <phrase>En tunn korsformad pekare.</phrase> </textobject> "
"</inlinemediaobject> Korspekaren:"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The cross hair pointer can be used to change the cell selection area. The "
"pointer appears when the mouse pointer is placed over the handle box, the "
"black square at the lower right hand side of the selection. When the cross "
"hair pointer appear, the selection can be altered by clicking the left-hand "
"mouse button and dragging the handle to a new position. The cross hair "
"pointer can also be used to insert a graphic object, by clicking with the "
"left hand mouse button to place one corner and releasing the button to place"
" another of the corners."
msgstr ""
"Korspekaren används för att ändra cellmarkeringen. Den visas när muspekaren "
"placeras över handtaget, den svarta rutan längst ned till höger om "
"markeringen. När korspekaren visas kan du ändra markeringen genom att hålla "
"ned vänster musknapp och dra handtaget till en ny plats. Du kan också "
"använda korspekaren för att infoga ett grafiskt objekt: klicka med vänster "
"musknapp där du vill placera ett hörn och släpp knappen vid nästa hörn."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/pointer_double_vertical_arrow.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> "
"</imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>A double ended vertical arrow.</phrase> "
"</textobject> </inlinemediaobject> <inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> "
"<imagedata fileref=\"figures/pointer_double_horizontal_arrow.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>A double ended "
"horizontal arrow.</phrase> </textobject> </inlinemediaobject> The expansion "
"pointers:"
msgstr ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/pointer_double_vertical_arrow.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> "
"</imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>En lodrät dubbelpil.</phrase> "
"</textobject> </inlinemediaobject> <inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> "
"<imagedata fileref=\"figures/pointer_double_horizontal_arrow.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>En vågrät "
"dubbelpil.</phrase> </textobject> </inlinemediaobject> Pekarna för "
"storleksändring:"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"These pointers can be used to change the height of rows or the width of "
"columns. These pointers appear in certain dialog windows to resize the "
"different parts of the dialog. The pointers are also used to resize "
"graphical objects as is explained below."
msgstr ""
"Med de här pekarna ändrar du radhöjd eller kolumnbredd. De visas också i "
"vissa dialogrutor när du ändrar storlek på rutans olika delar. Som beskrivs "
"nedan används pekarna även för att ändra storlek på grafiska objekt."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/pointer_hand_left.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> "
"<textobject> <phrase>A left pointing hand icon.</phrase> </textobject> "
"</inlinemediaobject> The sheet selection and hyperlink pointer:"
msgstr ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/pointer_hand_left.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> "
"<textobject> <phrase>En hand som pekar åt vänster.</phrase> </textobject> "
"</inlinemediaobject> Pekaren för bladval och hyperlänkar:"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"This pointer appears above the sheet tabs and can be used, by left clicking,"
" to change the currently selected sheet or, by right clicking, to obtain the"
" sheet dialog box. This pointer also appears above cells which are "
"hyperlinks. Left clicking on a hyperlink may change the view to a new "
"location, or may open an external file."
msgstr ""
"Den här pekaren visas över bladflikarna. Klicka med vänster musknapp för att"
" byta markerat blad eller med höger musknapp för att öppna bladdialogrutan. "
"Pekaren visas också över celler med hyperlänkar. Om du klickar på en "
"hyperlänk med vänster musknapp kan vyn ändras till en annan plats eller en "
"extern fil öppnas."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/pointer_right.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> "
"<textobject> <phrase>An arrow pointing to the upper right.</phrase> "
"</textobject> </inlinemediaobject> The right pointing arrow pointer:"
msgstr ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/pointer_right.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> "
"<textobject> <phrase>En pil som pekar snett uppåt åt höger.</phrase> "
"</textobject> </inlinemediaobject> Den högerpekande pilpekaren:"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The right hand pointing arrow pointer is used to select graphical objects "
"(such as drawing objects (e.g. arrows, ellipses) and graph objects (e.g. "
"charts))."
msgstr ""
"Den högerpekande pilpekaren används för att markera grafiska objekt, till "
"exempel ritobjekt (pilar och ellipser) och diagramobjekt."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/pointer_four_way_arrow.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> "
"</imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>A four way arrow.</phrase> </textobject>"
" </inlinemediaobject> The movement pointer:"
msgstr ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/pointer_four_way_arrow.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> "
"</imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>En pil med fyra spetsar.</phrase> "
"</textobject> </inlinemediaobject> Förflyttningspekaren:"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The movement pointer can be used to move graphical objects around a "
"worksheet without resizing the object."
msgstr ""
"Förflyttningspekaren används för att flytta grafiska objekt i kalkylbladet "
"utan att ändra deras storlek."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/pointer_double_vertical_arrow.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> "
"</imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>A double ended vertical arrow.</phrase> "
"</textobject> </inlinemediaobject> <inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> "
"<imagedata fileref=\"figures/pointer_double_horizontal_arrow.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>A double ended "
"horizontal arrow.</phrase> </textobject> </inlinemediaobject> "
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/pointer_diagonal_resize.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> "
"</imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>A diagonal double arrow with center "
"box.</phrase> </textobject> </inlinemediaobject> The graphical object re-"
"sizing pointers:"
msgstr ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/pointer_double_vertical_arrow.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> "
"</imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>En lodrät dubbelpil.</phrase> "
"</textobject> </inlinemediaobject> <inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> "
"<imagedata fileref=\"figures/pointer_double_horizontal_arrow.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>En vågrät "
"dubbelpil.</phrase> </textobject> </inlinemediaobject> <inlinemediaobject> "
"<imageobject> <imagedata fileref=\"figures/pointer_diagonal_resize.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>En diagonal dubbelpil "
"med en ruta i mitten.</phrase> </textobject> </inlinemediaobject> Pekare för"
" storleksändring av grafiska objekt:"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"These pointers allow the resizing of graphical objects. If the mouse pointer"
" is placed over one of the handle boxes of the graphical object, the handle "
"box will turn green and the pointer will change to one of these forms. When "
"these pointers appear, click dragging with the left mouse button will resize"
" the graphical object either scaling or stretching the object."
msgstr ""
"De här pekarna används för att ändra storlek på grafiska objekt. När du "
"placerar muspekaren över ett av objektets handtag blir handtaget grönt och "
"pekaren ändras till en av dessa former. Håll då ned vänster musknapp och dra"
" för att skala eller sträcka ut objektet."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/pointer_resize_multiple.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> "
"</imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>Several pointers used to resize dialogs "
"and windows.</phrase> </textobject> </inlinemediaobject> The window resizing"
" pointers:"
msgstr ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/pointer_resize_multiple.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> "
"</imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>Flera pekare som används för att ändra "
"storlek på dialogrutor och fönster.</phrase> </textobject> "
"</inlinemediaobject> Pekare för storleksändring av fönster:"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"These pointers are used to change the size of "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> windows and dialogs."
msgstr ""
"De här pekarna används för att ändra storlek på fönster och dialogrutor i "
"<application>Gnumeric</application>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"This chapter explains the core functionality of "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> including the basic types of data "
"manipulated by <application>Gnumeric</application>, the methods of entering,"
" manipulating and formatting data, and the basic tools for analysis of these"
" data. More advanced analysis is described in <xref linkend=\"chapter-"
"advanced-analysis\"/>."
msgstr ""
"Det här kapitlet beskriver grundfunktionerna i "
"<application>Gnumeric</application>, bland annat de grundläggande datatyper "
"som <application>Gnumeric</application> hanterar, hur du matar in, bearbetar"
" och formaterar data samt de viktigaste analysverktygen. Mer avancerad "
"analys beskrivs i <xref linkend=\"chapter-advanced-analysis\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The purpose of a spreadsheet is to manipulate data and perform calculations "
"on those data. In order to understand how to use "
"<application>Gnumeric</application>, it is necessary to understand what "
"types of data are available and how these types can be manipulated."
msgstr ""
"Ett kalkylblad används för att bearbeta data och utföra beräkningar. För att"
" förstå hur <application>Gnumeric</application> används behöver du känna "
"till vilka datatyper som finns och hur de kan bearbetas."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Because all of the data which are entered into a "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> workbook can eventually be stored in a "
"file, the file contents define the kinds of data which can be entered into "
"the spreadsheet. A file contains: <_:itemizedlist-1/> The metadata include a"
" brief document summary describing the file contents and include the "
"settings applicable to the data contents, such as the settings for the "
"printing of each sheet and any settings for automatically saving the file. "
"The global data for the workbook include any names which are defined by the "
"user and attributes, such as the protected status of the workbook and "
"sheets. The actual data contained in the worksheets include the contents of "
"the cells, both data and formatting, and other objects such as drawing and "
"charts."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom alla data i en <application>Gnumeric</application>-arbetsbok till "
"slut kan sparas i en fil avgör filens innehåll vilka slags data kalkylbladet"
" kan innehålla. En fil består av: <_:itemizedlist-1/> Metadata omfattar en "
"kort sammanfattning av filens innehåll och inställningar som gäller data, "
"till exempel utskriftsinställningar för varje blad och inställningar för "
"automatisk lagring. Arbetsbokens globala data omfattar användardefinierade "
"namn och egenskaper, exempelvis om arbetsboken och bladen är skyddade. De "
"faktiska kalkylbladsdata omfattar cellernas innehåll och formatering samt "
"andra objekt, såsom ritobjekt och diagram."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"This chapter describes the information which can be stored in spreadsheet "
"cells. This includes the five types of data which cells can contain and the "
"formatting which can be applied to each cell. The chapter first describes "
"the five data types available, then describes the formatting which can be "
"performed on each cell, then explains how data can be inserted into a "
"spreadsheet and finally describes how to copy and move data around a "
"worksheet along with the transformations which can be performed as the data "
"are moved. This chapter does not describe other types of data which can be "
"stored in a spreadsheet such as drawing elements and graphs used to chart "
"data. These are explained in later chapters."
msgstr ""
"Det här kapitlet beskriver vilka uppgifter som kan lagras i "
"kalkylbladsceller: de fem datatyperna och formateringen som kan användas för"
" varje cell. Först beskrivs datatyperna, sedan cellformateringen och hur "
"data matas in. Därefter förklaras hur du kopierar och flyttar data i "
"kalkylbladet och vilka omvandlingar som kan göras under flytten. Andra typer"
" av innehåll, till exempel ritobjekt och diagram, beskrivs i senare kapitel."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Each cell in a <application>Gnumeric</application> worksheet can contain "
"only a single data element. These elements will have one of five basic "
"types: text, numbers, booleans, formulas, or errors. During data entry, "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> assigns a default data type to the cell "
"based on an analysis of the cell contents. This assignment can be changed "
"later if <application>Gnumeric</application> makes the wrong assignment. For"
" information on how to change the data type of a cell, see <xref "
"linkend=\"sect-data-format\"/>."
msgstr ""
"Varje cell i ett <application>Gnumeric</application>-kalkylblad kan "
"innehålla ett enda dataelement av en av fem grundtyper: text, tal, booleska "
"värden, formler eller fel. När du matar in data tilldelar "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> cellen en datatyp utifrån innehållet. Om"
" <application>Gnumeric</application> väljer fel typ kan du ändra den senare."
" Se <xref linkend=\"sect-data-format\"/> om hur du ändrar datatyp för en "
"cell."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"A text element can contain a series of letters, numbers or other contents. "
"For example, the first cell in a worksheet might contain the characters "
"—This worksheet describes the company's income — which "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> would interpret to be text. In order to "
"distinguish text elements from number or formula elements, the text element "
"may start with a single quote. For instance, if a cell contained only the "
"three digits 345, <application>Gnumeric</application> would consider that to"
" be the number three hundred and forty five. If this cell is intended to be "
"a string, <application>Gnumeric</application> will store the cell as '345. "
"The newline character cannot be entered directly but must be entered as "
"<keycombo> <keycap>Alt</keycap> <keycap>Enter</keycap></keycombo>. For more "
"information on entering and formatting text elements, see <xref "
"linkend=\"sect-data-text\"/>."
msgstr ""
"Ett textelement kan bestå av bokstäver, siffror eller annat innehåll. Den "
"första cellen i ett kalkylblad kan till exempel innehålla texten ”Det här "
"kalkylbladet beskriver företagets intäkter”, som "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> tolkar som text. För att skilja "
"textelement från tal och formler kan texten inledas med en apostrof. Om en "
"cell till exempel bara innehåller siffrorna 345 tolkar "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> dem som talet trehundrafyrtiofem. Om "
"cellen i stället ska innehålla text lagrar "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> den som '345. Radbrytningar kan inte "
"matas in direkt, utan infogas med tangentkombinationen <keycombo> "
"<keycap>Alt</keycap> <keycap>Enter</keycap></keycombo>. Mer information om "
"hur du matar in och formaterar text finns i <xref linkend=\"sect-data-"
"text\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"A number element can contain a series of digits (425) but may include "
"specific text and formatting characters to indicate negative numbers (-345),"
" decimal separator (34.0567), thousand separators (12,342), currency ($23), "
"dates (21-10-1998), times (10:23) or scientific notation (2.3e12). Dates may"
" include the names of months or their abbreviation. The currency, decimal "
"separator and thousands separator symbols vary depending on the locale (the "
"language and other location specific behaviour) to which "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> has been set. See <xref linkend=\"sect-"
"configuration-localization\"/> to understand how to change the locale. If "
"you want a number to be displayed as a plain string without any number "
"formatting, you can put a single quote (') before it. For more information "
"on entering and formatting, numeric elements see <xref linkend=\"sect-data-"
"numbers\"/>."
msgstr ""
"Ett talelement kan bestå av siffror, som 425, och särskilda tecken för att "
"visa exempelvis negativa tal (-345), decimalavgränsare (34.0567), "
"tusentalsavgränsare (12,342), valuta ($23), datum (1998-10-21), klockslag "
"(10:23) eller vetenskaplig notation (2.3e12). Datum kan innehålla månadsnamn"
" eller förkortningar. Valuta-, decimal- och tusentalsavgränsare varierar "
"beroende på lokalen (språk och andra platsinställningar) som används i "
"<application>Gnumeric</application>. Se <xref linkend=\"sect-configuration-"
"localization\"/> om hur du ändrar lokalen. Om ett tal ska visas som vanlig "
"text utan talformatering kan du inleda det med en apostrof ('). Mer "
"information om hur du matar in och formaterar tal finns i <xref "
"linkend=\"sect-data-numbers\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"A boolean element can contain one of two values: TRUE and FALSE. These are "
"useful as inputs or outputs from formulas and for boolean algebra. More "
"information on boolean data elements is presented in <xref linkend=\"sect-"
"data-boolean\"/>."
msgstr ""
"Ett booleskt element kan ha ett av två värden: TRUE eller FALSE. Dessa "
"värden används som indata eller resultat i formler och inom boolesk algebra."
" Mer information om booleska dataelement finns i <xref linkend=\"sect-data-"
"boolean\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"A formula is an instruction to <application>Gnumeric</application> which "
"describes a calculation which should be performed automatically. These "
"formulas can contain standard arithmetic elements but can also contain "
"references to other cells. Calculations which depend on other cells are "
"usually recalculated when the values of another cell changes. Formulas "
"always begin with a special character — the equals sign (=). The commercial "
"at symbol (@) can be used instead of the equals sign during data entry but "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> will convert this to an equals sign. "
"Alternatively, an entry which describes a calculation and which starts with "
"either the plus (+) or minus symbol (-) will be converted to a formula "
"starting with an equals sign. For a more complete explanation of formulas, "
"see <xref linkend=\"sect-data-formulas\"/>."
msgstr ""
"En formel är en instruktion som anger vilken beräkning "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> ska utföra automatiskt. Formler kan "
"innehålla vanliga räkneoperationer och referenser till andra celler. "
"Beräkningar som beror på andra celler räknas vanligen om när värdet i någon "
"av dessa celler ändras. Formler börjar alltid med likhetstecknet (=). Under "
"inmatning kan tecknet @ användas i stället, men "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> omvandlar det till ett likhetstecken. "
"Även en inmatning som börjar med plus (+) eller minus (-) omvandlas till en "
"formel som börjar med likhetstecken. En utförligare förklaring av formler "
"finns i <xref linkend=\"sect-data-formulas\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"A cell reference is the part of a formula which refers to another cell. For "
"example, in the formula to add two cells =(A4+A1), both A4 and A1 are cell "
"references. These references can be quite complex referring to cells in "
"different worksheets or even in different files. See <xref linkend=\"sect-"
"data-formulas-references\"/> for a complete explanation of references."
msgstr ""
"En cellreferens är den del av en formel som hänvisar till en annan cell. I "
"formeln =(A4+A1), som summerar två celler, är både A4 och A1 cellreferenser."
" Referenser kan vara mer komplicerade och peka på celler i andra kalkylblad "
"eller till och med i andra filer. En fullständig förklaring finns i <xref "
"linkend=\"sect-data-formulas-references\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"An error element describes the failure to calculate the result of a formula."
" These values are rarely entered directly by a user but usually are the "
"display given when a formula cannot be correctly calculated. See <xref "
"linkend=\"sect-data-errors\"/> for a complete list of error values and their"
" explanation."
msgstr ""
"Ett felvärde anger att resultatet av en formel inte kunde beräknas. "
"Användaren skriver sällan in sådana värden direkt; de visas vanligen när en "
"formel inte kan beräknas korrekt. En fullständig lista över felvärden och "
"deras betydelse finns i <xref linkend=\"sect-data-errors\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The five basic types of data which can be stored in a spreadsheet cell are: "
"<_:variablelist-1/>"
msgstr ""
"De fem grundläggande datatyper som kan lagras i en kalkylbladscell är: "
"<_:variablelist-1/>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"A cell may display a series of hash marks (######). This indicates that the "
"result is too wide to display in the cell given the current font setting and"
" the current column width. When this occurs, the value in the cell can be "
"seen in two ways. If the cell is selected, the value will appear in the data"
" entry area (to the right of the equals button directly above the cell "
"grid). Alternatively, the column containing the cell can be widened until "
"the data contents become visible: select the whole column (by clicking on "
"the column header) and choose <menuchoice> <guimenu>Format</guimenu> "
"<guisubmenu>Column</guisubmenu> <guimenuitem>Auto fit "
"selection</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."
msgstr ""
"En cell kan visa flera nummertecken (######). Det betyder att resultatet är "
"för brett för att visas med den aktuella teckenstorleken och kolumnbredden. "
"Du kan se cellens värde på två sätt. Markera cellen så visas värdet i "
"inmatningsfältet, till höger om likhetsteckenknappen ovanför cellrutnätet. "
"Du kan också bredda kolumnen tills innehållet syns: markera hela kolumnen "
"genom att klicka på kolumnrubriken och välj <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Format</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Kolumn</guisubmenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Autopassa markering</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Text elements consist of an arbitrary sequence of characters or numbers "
"entered into a cell. Because <application>Gnumeric</application> "
"automatically recognizes certain sequences as numbers or formulas, certain "
"sequences of characters (such as sequences containing only digits or a text "
"element which starts with an equals sign) must be treated specially to have "
"them considered text. In order to force any sequence to be considered text, "
"the sequence can be started with an apostrophe symbol (<keysym>'</keysym>). "
"Alternatively, the 'number' format of the cell can be specified to be 'text'"
" before entering the characters, as explained in <xref linkend=\"number-"
"formatting-overview\"/>. Text elements are the simplest elements to enter "
"into spreadsheet cells."
msgstr ""
"Textelement består av en valfri följd tecken eller siffror som matas in i en"
" cell. Eftersom <application>Gnumeric</application> automatiskt känner igen "
"vissa följder som tal eller formler måste vissa inmatningar behandlas "
"särskilt för att tolkas som text, till exempel en följd som bara innehåller "
"siffror eller börjar med ett likhetstecken. Inled inmatningen med en "
"apostrof (<keysym>'</keysym>) för att tvinga den att tolkas som text. Du kan"
" också ändra cellens talformat till ”text” innan du skriver in tecknen, "
"enligt beskrivningen i <xref linkend=\"number-formatting-overview\"/>. "
"Textelement är det enklaste att mata in i kalkylbladsceller."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"An example of a spreadsheet cell grid with cells containing text is given in"
" <xref linkend=\"fig-cell-with-text\"/>. <_:figure-1/>"
msgstr ""
"<xref linkend=\"fig-cell-with-text\"/> visar ett exempel på ett cellrutnät "
"med text i cellerna. <_:figure-1/>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Valid text entries include simple words, whole sentences and even "
"paragraphs."
msgstr ""
"Text kan bestå av enstaka ord, hela meningar eller till och med stycken."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"To include a newline in a cell, a special key combination is required. A "
"newline symbol can be inserted with the key combination of "
"<keycombo><keysym>Alt</keysym><keysym>Enter</keysym></keycombo>."
msgstr ""
"Du behöver en särskild tangentkombination för att infoga en radbrytning i en"
" cell. Använd "
"<keycombo><keysym>Alt</keysym><keysym>Enter</keysym></keycombo>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Number data elements include a variety of data all of which are stored and "
"manipulated by <application>Gnumeric</application> as numbers. This includes"
" integers, decimal fractions, general fractions, numbers in scientific "
"notation, dates, times, and currency values."
msgstr ""
"Talelement omfattar flera slags värden som "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> lagrar och bearbetar som tal: heltal, "
"decimaltal, vanliga bråk, tal i vetenskaplig notation, datum, klockslag och "
"valutavärden."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Data are recognized as numbers when they are entered, dependent on the "
"format of the sequence of characters entered. "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> attempts to intelligently guess the "
"subtype of the data and match the data to an existing format for numbered "
"data. If it matches a data format, <application>Gnumeric</application> will "
"automatically assign the datum to a data type and associate an appropriate "
"display format with the cell. The format recognition of "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> includes a wide variety of data formats "
"which are discussed in detail in <xref linkend=\"number-formatting-"
"overview\"/>."
msgstr ""
"Inmatade data tolkas som tal beroende på hur tecknen är formaterade. "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> försöker avgöra vilken undertyp data har"
" och matcha dem mot ett befintligt talformat. Om ett format känns igen "
"tilldelar <application>Gnumeric</application> automatiskt data en datatyp "
"och kopplar ett lämpligt visningsformat till cellen. "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> känner igen många olika format, som "
"beskrivs närmare i <xref linkend=\"number-formatting-overview\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Because <application>Gnumeric</application> automatically guesses the data "
"type of a number being entered into a cell, this process may have to be "
"over-ridden for certain types of data. For example, postal codes in the "
"United States consist of a sequence of numbers which "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> interprets as an integer. However, U.S. "
"postal codes can start with a leading zero which "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> discards by default. In order to "
"override the default format, the number format of the cell must be specified"
" before the entry of the data. This is explained in <xref linkend=\"number-"
"formatting-overview\"/>, below."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom <application>Gnumeric</application> automatiskt gissar datatypen "
"för ett tal som matas in kan du behöva åsidosätta den för vissa slags data. "
"Postnummer i USA består till exempel av siffror som "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> tolkar som heltal. Amerikanska "
"postnummer kan dock börja med noll, som <application>Gnumeric</application> "
"tar bort som standard. Om du vill behålla nollan måste du ange cellens "
"talformat innan du matar in värdet. Detta beskrivs nedan i <xref "
"linkend=\"number-formatting-overview\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Cells can contain boolean data elements. These elements arise from Boolean "
"logic which is a branch of mathematics. These elements are useful for "
"manipulation of formulas."
msgstr ""
"Celler kan innehålla booleska dataelement. De bygger på boolesk logik, en "
"gren av matematiken, och används vid hantering av formler."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Boolean values can be either \"TRUE\" or \"FALSE\". If these strings are "
"entered into a cell, <application>Gnumeric</application> will recognize "
"these as boolean values. These values can then be used in formulas. Certain "
"formulas will also return boolean values."
msgstr ""
"Booleska värden kan vara ”TRUE” eller ”FALSE”. Om du skriver in någon av "
"dessa strängar i en cell känner <application>Gnumeric</application> igen den"
" som ett booleskt värde. Värdena kan sedan användas i formler, och vissa "
"formler returnerar också booleska värden."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Formulas are the key to making a powerful spreadsheet. A formula instructs "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> to perform calculations and display the "
"results. These calculations are defined as a formula data elements. The "
"power of these formulas arises because these formulas can include the "
"contents of other cells and the results of the formulas are updated "
"automatically when the contents of any cell included in the formula change. "
"The contents of other cells are included using \"cell references\" which are"
" explained below."
msgstr ""
"Formler gör kalkylblad kraftfulla. En formel instruerar "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> att utföra en beräkning och visa "
"resultatet. Formler kan använda innehållet i andra celler, och resultatet "
"uppdateras automatiskt när innehållet i någon av dessa celler ändras. Du "
"hänvisar till andra celler med cellreferenser, som beskrivs nedan."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Any formula entered into a cell must follow a specific syntax so that "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> can interpret the formula correctly. "
"This syntax closely follows mathematical notation but also includes "
"spreadsheet formulas, object names and cell references."
msgstr ""
"Formler som matas in i en cell måste följa en viss syntax för att "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> ska kunna tolka dem rätt. Syntaxen "
"följer i stort matematisk notation men omfattar också kalkylbladsformler, "
"objektnamn och cellreferenser."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Formulas are distinguished from regular data by starting with an equals sign"
" (=) as the first character. Everything following this equals sign is "
"evaluated as a formula."
msgstr ""
"Formler skiljs från vanliga data genom att börja med ett likhetstecken (=). "
"Allt som följer efter tecknet tolkas som en formel."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"To accommodate those more familiar with Lotus spreadsheets, Gnumeric "
"recognizes the commercial at symbol (@) as the beginning of a formula and "
"substitutes an equals sign. The plus and minus characters (+ and -) may also"
" start formulas that involve calculation, but when used in front of a single"
" number only indicate the sign of the number."
msgstr ""
"För att underlätta för användare som är vana vid Lotus-kalkylblad känner "
"Gnumeric igen snabel-a (@) som början på en formel och byter ut det mot ett "
"likhetstecken. Plus- och minustecknen (+ och -) kan också inleda beräknande "
"formler, men framför ett ensamt tal anger de bara talets tecken."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The simplest formulas just use the standard math operator and symbols. "
"Addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division are represented by +, -,"
" *, and /, just as you would expect. +,- can be placed in front of numbers "
"to indicate sign, as well. <_:example-1/>"
msgstr ""
"De enklaste formlerna använder vanliga matematiska operatorer och symboler. "
"Addition, subtraktion, multiplikation och division skrivs med +, -, * "
"respektive /. Plus- och minustecken kan också stå framför tal för att ange "
"deras tecken. <_:example-1/>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Formulas can result in error values in several instances. If a formula is "
"entered incorrectly, <application>Gnumeric</application> will display a "
"warning and allow either the formula to be corrected or will save the "
"formula as text for editing later. If a syntactically correct formula "
"results in a nonsensical calculation (for instance, a division by zero), "
"then an error value will be displayed indicating the error."
msgstr ""
"Formler kan ge felvärden av flera orsaker. Om en formel är felaktigt inmatad"
" visar <application>Gnumeric</application> en varning och låter dig antingen"
" rätta formeln eller spara den som text för senare redigering. Om en formel "
"har korrekt syntax men ger en orimlig beräkning, till exempel division med "
"noll, visas ett felvärde som anger felet."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Formulas can also contain functions which denote the use of standard "
"mathematical, business, statistical, and scientific calculations. These "
"functions take the place of any data element in a formula and can therefore "
"be combined with the standard arithmetic operators described above."
msgstr ""
"Formler kan också innehålla funktioner för vanliga matematiska, ekonomiska, "
"statistiska och naturvetenskapliga beräkningar. Funktioner kan ersätta ett "
"dataelement i en formel och kombineras med de vanliga räkneoperatorerna "
"ovan."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"These functions have the form: <_:example-1/> where FUNCTIONNAME indicates "
"the name of a function and ARGUMENTS indicates one or more arguments to the "
"function. The function arguments are separated by commas "
"(<keysym>,</keysym>)."
msgstr ""
"Funktioner skrivs på formen <_:example-1/>, där FUNCTIONNAME är funktionens "
"namn och ARGUMENTS är ett eller flera argument. Funktionsargument avgränsas "
"med kommatecken (<keysym>,</keysym>)."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"While the documentation generally refers to functions and to cells in "
"capital letters, their use is not actually case sensitive."
msgstr ""
"Även om dokumentationen oftast skriver funktionsnamn och cellreferenser med "
"versaler gör Gnumeric ingen skillnad på stora och små bokstäver."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Some examples of the use of functions are: <_:example-1/> The arguments of "
"the functions vary in number from none, as in the PI() function, to an "
"unlimited number, as in the SUM() function, depending on the type of "
"function."
msgstr ""
"Här följer några exempel på funktioner: <_:example-1/> Antalet argument "
"varierar beroende på funktionen: PI() tar inga argument, medan SUM() kan ta "
"hur många som helst."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Formulas can include the displayed data from other cells. These contents are"
" described as `cell references' which are names indicating that the contents"
" of other cells should be used in the calculation."
msgstr ""
"Formler kan använda värden som visas i andra celler. Dessa anges med "
"cellreferenser, alltså namn som talar om att innehållet i andra celler ska "
"ingå i beräkningen."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Each cell in a spreadsheet is named by its column and row labels. By "
"default, the column labels are letters and the row labels are numbers. The "
"first cell, therefore, is called A1. One column over and two rows down from "
"cell A1 is the cell B3. In a worksheet of the default size, the right most "
"and bottom most cell is cell IV65536 which is the cell in column IV and in "
"row 65536. An alternative cell reference notation uses numbers for both row "
"and column identification. See <xref linkend=\"sect-data-formulas-"
"references-r1c1\"/> below for details."
msgstr ""
"Varje cell i ett kalkylblad identifieras med kolumn- och radrubriken. "
"Kolumner betecknas som standard med bokstäver och rader med siffror. Den "
"första cellen heter därför A1. Cellen en kolumn åt höger och två rader ned "
"från A1 är B3. I ett kalkylblad med standardstorlek är den nedersta cellen "
"längst till höger IV65536, i kolumn IV och rad 65536. Det finns också en "
"referensnotation där både kolumn och rad anges med siffror. Mer information "
"finns nedan i <xref linkend=\"sect-data-formulas-references-r1c1\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The value of a cell can be used in a formula simply by entering its name "
"where a number value would otherwise occur. For example, to have the data in"
" cell B1 appear in another cell, enter =B1 into that cell. Other more "
"complex examples include: <_:example-1/>"
msgstr ""
"Du kan använda en cells värde i en formel genom att skriva cellens namn där "
"ett tal annars skulle stå. Om du till exempel vill visa innehållet i B1 i en"
" annan cell skriver du =B1 där. Här följer några mer avancerade exempel: "
"<_:example-1/>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Cells can be referenced in the default way (relative referencing), or by "
"using absolute referencing. Absolute referencing means that when the cell is"
" copied, the cell reference does not change. Normally, auto-filling a cell "
"range or moving a cell will change its cell reference so that it maintains a"
" relation to the original cell. Absolute referencing prevents these changes."
msgstr ""
"Celler kan refereras relativt, vilket är standard, eller absolut. En absolut"
" referens ändras inte när cellen kopieras. Normalt ändras cellreferenser när"
" du autofyller ett cellområde eller flyttar en cell, så att de behåller "
"relationen till ursprungscellen. Absoluta referenser förhindrar detta."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The difference between absolute and relative cell references only matters if"
" you are copying or moving cells that contain cell references. For cells "
"that are going to remain in place, both the relative and absolute references"
" have the same result."
msgstr ""
"Skillnaden mellan absoluta och relativa cellreferenser spelar bara roll när "
"du kopierar eller flyttar celler som innehåller referenser. Om cellerna står"
" kvar på samma plats ger båda typerna samma resultat."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"For example, if =A1 is the formula entered into cell B2, cell B2 will "
"display the data in cell A1, which is one row up and one column left. Then, "
"if you copy the contents of B2 to cell F6, cell F6 will contain the value "
"from E5, which is also one row up and one column left."
msgstr ""
"Om formeln =A1 till exempel matas in i B2 visar cellen innehållet i A1, som "
"ligger en rad upp och en kolumn till vänster. Om du sedan kopierar "
"innehållet i B2 till F6 hämtar F6 värdet från E5, som också ligger en rad "
"upp och en kolumn till vänster."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"For the copied cell to still refer to A1, specify absolute references using "
"the $ character: $A$1 refers to cell A1, no matter where it is copied."
msgstr ""
"Om den kopierade cellen fortfarande ska hänvisa till A1 anger du en absolut "
"referens med dollartecknet: $A$1 hänvisar till A1 oavsett var formeln "
"kopieras."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The format for absolute cell referencing is to use a '$' in front of the "
"cell coordinate that you want to stay constant. The column, the row, or both"
" can be held constant."
msgstr ""
"Du anger en absolut cellreferens genom att sätta ett ”$” framför den del av "
"cellkoordinaten som ska vara konstant. Du kan låsa kolumnen, raden eller "
"båda."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"=A1 is a normal, or relative, cell reference function. When =A1 is entered "
"into cell B2, it refers to the value of data one cell up and one cell left "
"from the cell with the reference. Therefore, if this formula were copied "
"from cell B2 to cell C2, the value displayed in cell C2 will be the value of"
" data in cell B1. Copied to cell R19, the formula will display the data in "
"cell Q18."
msgstr ""
"=A1 är en vanlig, relativ cellreferens. Om du skriver =A1 i B2 hämtas värdet"
" från cellen en rad upp och en kolumn till vänster. Om formeln kopieras från"
" B2 till C2 visar C2 därför värdet från B1. Om den kopieras till R19 visas "
"värdet från Q18."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"In this case, the column value is absolute, but the row value is relative. "
"Therefore, if =$A1 is entered into cell B2, the formula refers to the data "
"in column A that is one row up from the current location. Copied to cell C2,"
" the formula will refer to the data in cell A1. Copied to cell R19, it will "
"refer to the data in A18."
msgstr ""
"Här är kolumnen absolut, men raden relativ. Om du skriver =$A1 i B2 hänvisar"
" formeln till data i kolumn A, en rad ovanför den aktuella platsen. Kopierar"
" du formeln till C2 hänvisar den till A1. Kopierar du den till R19 hänvisar "
"den till A18."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"This formula uses a relative column value and an absolute row value. In cell"
" B2, it refers to cell A1 as the data in the cell one column left and in row"
" 1. Copied to cell C3, the formula will display the data in cell B1."
msgstr ""
"Den här formeln har en relativ kolumn och en absolut rad. I B2 hänvisar den "
"till A1, alltså cellen en kolumn till vänster på rad 1. Om formeln kopieras "
"till C3 visar den innehållet i B1."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"No matter where this formula is copied, it will always refer to the data in "
"cell A1."
msgstr "Oavsett var formeln kopieras hänvisar den alltid till data i A1."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"What happens when a given formula is entered into cell B2, then copied to "
"other cells? <_:variablelist-1/>"
msgstr ""
"Vad händer när en formel skrivs in i B2 och sedan kopieras till andra "
"celler? <_:variablelist-1/>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"From the <guimenuitem>Format ▶ Sheet</guimenuitem> submenu you can select "
"R1C1 notation for a worksheet. This causes all cell references on the sheet "
"to be shown as “R<emphasis role=\"italic\">r</emphasis>C<emphasis "
"role=\"italic\">c</emphasis>”, where <emphasis role=\"italic\">r</emphasis> "
"is the row number and <emphasis role=\"italic\">c</emphasis> is the column "
"number. When R1C1 notation is selected, the column headers show numbers "
"rather than letters."
msgstr ""
"I undermenyn <guimenuitem>Format ▶ Blad</guimenuitem> kan du välja "
"R1C1-notation för ett kalkylblad. Då visas alla cellreferenser på bladet som"
" ”R<emphasis role=\"italic\">r</emphasis>C<emphasis "
"role=\"italic\">c</emphasis>”, där <emphasis role=\"italic\">r</emphasis> är"
" radnumret och <emphasis role=\"italic\">c</emphasis> kolumnnumret. Med "
"R1C1-notation visas kolumnrubrikerna som siffror i stället för bokstäver."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"When <emphasis role=\"italic\">r</emphasis> and <emphasis "
"role=\"italic\">c</emphasis> are positive integers, as in “R1C1”, the "
"reference is absolute. To produce a relative reference, enclose a number in "
"square brackets; if the number is zero, it can be omitted along with the "
"brackets. For example, “RC[-2]” refers to the cell two columns to the left "
"in the current row, while “R[1]C1” refers to the cell in the first column of"
" the next row down from the referencing cell. The second example combines a "
"relative row reference with an absolute column reference."
msgstr ""
"När <emphasis role=\"italic\">r</emphasis> och <emphasis "
"role=\"italic\">c</emphasis> är positiva heltal, som i ”R1C1”, är referensen"
" absolut. Skapa en relativ referens genom att sätta ett tal inom "
"hakparenteser. Om talet är noll kan det och hakparenteserna utelämnas. "
"”RC[-2]” hänvisar till cellen två kolumner till vänster på den aktuella "
"raden, medan ”R[1]C1” hänvisar till cellen i den första kolumnen på raden "
"under referenscellen. Det senare exemplet kombinerar en relativ radreferens "
"med en absolut kolumnreferens."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Many functions can take multiple cells as arguments. This can either be a "
"comma separated list, an array, or any combination thereof."
msgstr ""
"Många funktioner kan ta flera celler som argument. Du kan ange dem som en "
"kommaseparerad lista, en matris eller en kombination av dessa."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"A comma separated list of cell references can be used to indicate cells that"
" are discontinuous."
msgstr ""
"Använd en kommaseparerad lista med cellreferenser för att ange celler som "
"inte ligger intill varandra."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"For functions that take more than one argument, it is often easier to "
"reference the cells as a group. This can include cells in sets horizontally,"
" vertically, or in arrays."
msgstr ""
"För funktioner som tar flera argument är det ofta enklare att ange cellerna "
"som ett område. Området kan bestå av celler i en vågrät eller lodrät följd, "
"eller av en matris."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The ':' operator is used to indicate a range of cells. The basic syntax is "
"upper left corner:bottom right corner."
msgstr ""
"Kolonoperatorn ”:” anger ett cellområde. Grundformen är övre vänstra "
"hörnet:nedre högra hörnet."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"For referencing cells that are in non-continuous regions, you can use any "
"combination of the above methods to get the needed cells."
msgstr ""
"Du kan kombinera metoderna ovan för att referera till celler i flera "
"åtskilda områden."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"It is possible to reference cells which are not part of the current sheet. "
"This is done using the SHEETNAME!CELLLIST syntax, where SHEETNAME is an "
"identifier (usually a sheet name) and CELLLIST is a reference to a cell or "
"range of cells as described in the previous sections. If SHEETNAME contains "
"spaces or other special characters, you must quote the whole name to allow "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> to recognize it as a single name. See "
"the examples below."
msgstr ""
"Du kan referera till celler på andra blad med syntaxen SHEETNAME!CELLLIST. "
"SHEETNAME är en identifierare, oftast ett bladnamn, och CELLLIST är en "
"referens till en cell eller ett cellområde enligt beskrivningen ovan. Om "
"SHEETNAME innehåller blanksteg eller andra specialtecken måste du omge hela "
"namnet med citattecken så att <application>Gnumeric</application> tolkar det"
" som ett enda namn. Se exemplen nedan."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"When the reference is to a range of cells, the worksheet name only needs to "
"be given with the first cell reference. The ending cell of the range is "
"assumed to be on the same worksheet if an explicit sheet name is not "
"specified. Note, however, that “Sheet1!A1:Sheet3!C5” is a legitimate cell "
"range description. It identifies a range three columns wide and five rows "
"deep on each of the worksheets from Sheet1 through Sheet3. The preferred "
"form of such a reference is “Sheet1:Sheet3!A1:C5”, which is the form "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> will display if you subsequently edit "
"the contents of a cell containing such a reference."
msgstr ""
"När du refererar till ett cellområde behöver bladnamnet bara anges vid den "
"första cellreferensen. Om inget bladnamn anges för den sista cellen antas "
"den ligga på samma blad. Observera att ”Sheet1!A1:Sheet3!C5” är en giltig "
"områdesreferens. Den anger ett område som är tre kolumner brett och fem "
"rader högt på varje blad från Sheet1 till Sheet3. Den rekommenderade formen "
"är ”Sheet1:Sheet3!A1:C5”. Det är den form "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> visar om du senare redigerar en cell med"
" en sådan referens."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"It is possible to reference cells in other files. The canonical form for "
"these references is [<emphasis "
"role=\"italic\">filename</emphasis>]SHEETNAME!CELLLIST. The square brackets "
"serve to quote <emphasis role=\"italic\">filename</emphasis>, so you should "
"use quotation marks only if they are actually part of the file name. Note "
"that the sheet name must be present in references of this form."
msgstr ""
"Det går också att referera till celler i andra filer. Standardformen är "
"[<emphasis role=\"italic\">filename</emphasis>]SHEETNAME!CELLLIST. "
"Hakparenteserna avgränsar <emphasis role=\"italic\">filename</emphasis>, så "
"använd citattecken bara om de faktiskt ingår i filnamnet. Observera att "
"bladnamnet måste finnas med i den här typen av referens."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Names are labels which have a meaning defined in the spreadsheet or by "
"<application>Gnumeric</application>. A name can refer to a numeric value, a "
"string, a range of cells, or a formula. For details on defining and using "
"names, see <xref linkend=\"sect-data-names\"/>."
msgstr ""
"Namn är beteckningar vars betydelse definieras i kalkylbladet eller av "
"<application>Gnumeric</application>. Ett namn kan hänvisa till ett talvärde,"
" en textsträng, ett cellområde eller en formel. Mer information om hur du "
"definierar och använder namn finns i <xref linkend=\"sect-data-names\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"It is periodically useful or necessary to have an expression return a matrix"
" rather than a single value. The first example most people think of are "
"matrix operations such as multiplication, transpose, and inverse. A less "
"obvious usage is for data retrieval routines (databases, realtime data-"
"feeds) or functions with vector results (yield curve calculations)."
msgstr ""
"Ibland behöver ett uttryck returnera en matris i stället för ett enskilt "
"värde. Vanliga exempel är matrisoperationer som multiplikation, "
"transponering och invertering. Matriser kan också användas mindre uppenbart,"
" till exempel för att hämta data från databaser eller dataströmmar i "
"realtid, eller i funktioner som ger vektorresultat, såsom beräkningar av "
"avkastningskurvor."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"An array formula is currently entered by selecting the single range in which"
" to store the result, entering the array formula, and hitting the key "
"combination, <keycombo> <keycap>Ctrl</keycap> <keycap>Shift</keycap> "
"<keycap>Enter</keycap> </keycombo>."
msgstr ""
"Du anger en matrisformel genom att först markera det område där resultatet "
"ska placeras, skriva formeln och sedan trycka på <keycombo> "
"<keycap>Ctrl</keycap> <keycap>Shift</keycap> <keycap>Enter</keycap> "
"</keycombo>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Solely for compatibility with Excel and ODF files, "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> supports various database functions: "
"<xref linkend=\"gnumeric-function-DAVERAGE\"/>, <xref linkend=\"gnumeric-"
"function-DCOUNT\"/>, <xref linkend=\"gnumeric-function-DCOUNTA\"/>, <xref "
"linkend=\"gnumeric-function-DGET\"/>, <xref linkend=\"gnumeric-function-"
"DMAX\"/>, <xref linkend=\"gnumeric-function-DMIN\"/>, <xref "
"linkend=\"gnumeric-function-DPRODUCT\"/>, <xref linkend=\"gnumeric-function-"
"DSTDEV\"/>, <xref linkend=\"gnumeric-function-DSTDEVP\"/>, <xref "
"linkend=\"gnumeric-function-DSUM\"/>, <xref linkend=\"gnumeric-function-"
"DVAR\"/> and <xref linkend=\"gnumeric-function-DVARP\"/>."
msgstr ""
"Enbart för kompatibilitet med Excel- och ODF-filer stöder "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> flera databasfunktioner: <xref "
"linkend=\"gnumeric-function-DAVERAGE\"/>, <xref linkend=\"gnumeric-function-"
"DCOUNT\"/>, <xref linkend=\"gnumeric-function-DCOUNTA\"/>, <xref "
"linkend=\"gnumeric-function-DGET\"/>, <xref linkend=\"gnumeric-function-"
"DMAX\"/>, <xref linkend=\"gnumeric-function-DMIN\"/>, <xref "
"linkend=\"gnumeric-function-DPRODUCT\"/>, <xref linkend=\"gnumeric-function-"
"DSTDEV\"/>, <xref linkend=\"gnumeric-function-DSTDEVP\"/>, <xref "
"linkend=\"gnumeric-function-DSUM\"/>, <xref linkend=\"gnumeric-function-"
"DVAR\"/> och <xref linkend=\"gnumeric-function-DVARP\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Since these functions are quite restrictive on the criteria that can be "
"used, it is often easier to use array functions as described in <xref "
"linkend=\"sect-data-formulas-array\"/>. Array functions are also useful in "
"the case that a specific database function does not exist:"
msgstr ""
"Eftersom dessa funktioner begränsar vilka villkor som kan användas är det "
"ofta enklare att använda matrisfunktioner, som beskrivs i <xref "
"linkend=\"sect-data-formulas-array\"/>. Matrisfunktioner är också användbara"
" när en viss databasfunktion saknas:"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Cells can display error values if the formula contained in the cell cannot "
"be solved or if other anomalous conditions occur."
msgstr ""
"Celler kan visa felvärden om formeln i cellen inte går att beräkna eller om "
"andra avvikande förhållanden uppstår."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"In <application>Gnumeric</application> all error values have names that "
"start with <code>#</code>. 8 error values are standardized:"
msgstr ""
"I <application>Gnumeric</application> börjar alla felvärden med "
"<code>#</code>. Åtta felvärden är standardiserade:"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The result of specifying an intersecting range that in fact does "
"<emphasis>not</emphasis> intersect."
msgstr ""
"Resultatet när ett angivet skärningsområde i själva verket "
"<emphasis>inte</emphasis> skär varandra."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"A formula could not be evaluated because an invalid number was used as "
"argument, for example <code>=SQRT(-1)</code>"
msgstr ""
"Formeln kunde inte beräknas eftersom ett ogiltigt tal användes som argument,"
" till exempel <code>=SQRT(-1)</code>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Usually the result of importing an unrecognized error from a different file "
"format."
msgstr ""
"Visas vanligtvis när ett okänt fel importeras från ett annat filformat."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"A formula could not be evaluated because the wrong type of argument was "
"used."
msgstr ""
"Formeln kunde inte beräknas eftersom ett argument av fel typ användes."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"There are several ways to add data into a spreadsheet. The simplest data "
"entry technique involves typing the data into a spreadsheet by hand. This is"
" usually necessary the first time that data are introduced into a computer. "
"If the data already exist in a computer file of some kind, a simple way "
"might exist to insert these data into a <application>Gnumeric</application> "
"worksheet. If the data are in a text file, they can be inserted into a "
"worksheet rapidly using the text conversion facilities. If data exist in a "
"spreadsheet file of a different format, <application>Gnumeric</application> "
"may be able to open the file and the data can then be copied where they are "
"wanted."
msgstr ""
"Det finns flera sätt att lägga in data i ett kalkylblad. Det enklaste är att"
" skriva in dem för hand, vilket oftast behövs när data matas in i en dator "
"för första gången. Om data redan finns i en fil kan det finnas ett enkelt "
"sätt att föra in dem i ett <application>Gnumeric</application>-kalkylblad. "
"Textfiler kan snabbt importeras med verktygen för textkonvertering. Om data "
"finns i ett kalkylblad med ett annat filformat kan "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> kanske öppna filen, så att du sedan kan "
"kopiera data dit de behövs."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"This section explains how to enter data by hand into a spreadsheet. The "
"techniques necessary to obtain data from other computer sources are "
"explained in <xref linkend=\"chapter-files\"/> which deals with external "
"data sources."
msgstr ""
"Det här avsnittet beskriver hur du matar in data för hand i ett kalkylblad. "
"Hur du hämtar data från andra källor beskrivs i <xref linkend=\"chapter-"
"files\"/>, som handlar om externa datakällor."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"If the information being entered into <application>Gnumeric</application> "
"cannot be interpreted correctly, <application>Gnumeric</application> will "
"display an error message. The user may then be forced to edit the data "
"before continuing. For example, a formula may be mathematically incorrect if"
" the user has two operators in a row (e.g. =3+*4) and the dialog will give "
"the user the chance to re-edit the entry or accept the entry as text rather "
"than as a formula. When the formula is corrected, the leading apostrophe can"
" be removed and <application>Gnumeric</application> will re-interpret the "
"entry as a formula."
msgstr ""
"Om <application>Gnumeric</application> inte kan tolka inmatad information "
"korrekt visar <application>Gnumeric</application> ett felmeddelande. Du kan "
"behöva redigera data innan du fortsätter. En formel blir till exempel "
"matematiskt felaktig om två operatorer står efter varandra (till exempel "
"=3+*4). Dialogrutan låter dig då redigera inmatningen eller godta den som "
"text i stället för som formel. När formeln har rättats kan du ta bort den "
"inledande apostrofen, så tolkar <application>Gnumeric</application> "
"inmatningen som en formel igen."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The simplest method to place data in a spreadsheet involves selecting the "
"location for the data, typing the data on a keyboard and then typing the "
"<keysym>Enter</keysym> key to finish the input."
msgstr ""
"Det enklaste sättet att lägga in data är att markera en cell, skriva in data"
" med tangentbordet och trycka på <keysym>Enter</keysym> för att avsluta "
"inmatningen."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Select the cell where you want to enter data by clicking on it with the "
"white cross cursor. This will place the thick `selection' box around that "
"cell."
msgstr ""
"Klicka med den vita korspekaren på cellen där du vill mata in data. En tjock"
" markeringsram visas runt cellen."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Type in the data or formula. The details of this step are presented below "
"for each of the five types of data which can be entered."
msgstr ""
"Skriv in data eller en formel. Nedan beskrivs hur du gör för var och en av "
"de fem datatyperna."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Press the <keysym>Enter</keysym> key. This will complete the input and move "
"the selection box down one cell which will then be able to receive further "
"input."
msgstr ""
"Tryck på <keysym>Enter</keysym>. Då avslutas inmatningen och markeringen "
"flyttas ned en cell, så att du kan fortsätta mata in data."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"At any time while entering the data and before the <keysym>Enter</keysym> is"
" pressed, the user can cancel the data entry by typing the "
"<keysym>Esc</keysym> key. This will return the spreadsheet to the selection "
"mode and restore the contents previously in the selected cell."
msgstr ""
"Du kan när som helst innan du trycker på <keysym>Enter</keysym> avbryta "
"inmatningen genom att trycka på <keysym>Esc</keysym>. Då återgår "
"kalkylbladet till markeringsläget och cellens tidigare innehåll återställs."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Instead of the <keysym>Enter</keysym> key, other keys can be used to input "
"the data in the current cell. These other keys will move the selection box "
"to other locations than does the <keysym>Enter</keysym> key. The "
"<keysym>Tab</keysym> key inputs the entry in the currently selected cell and"
" then moves the selection box one cell to the right of the current cell. The"
" arrow keys input the entry into the currently selected cell and move one "
"cell in the direction of the arrow. The <keysym>Enter</keysym> key can also "
"be used in conjunction with other keys. Typing the "
"<keycombo><keysym>Shift</keysym><keysym>Enter</keysym></keycombo> "
"combination will move the selection upwards after entry. Typing the "
"<keycombo><keysym>Ctrl</keysym><keysym>Enter</keysym></keycombo> combination"
" will re-select the currently selected cell."
msgstr ""
"Du kan använda andra tangenter än <keysym>Enter</keysym> för att mata in "
"data i den aktuella cellen och flytta markeringen på andra sätt än med "
"<keysym>Enter</keysym>. <keysym>Tab</keysym> matar in värdet i den markerade"
" cellen och flyttar markeringen en cell åt höger. Piltangenterna matar in "
"värdet och flyttar markeringen en cell i pilens riktning. Du kan också "
"kombinera <keysym>Enter</keysym> med andra tangenter. "
"<keycombo><keysym>Shift</keysym><keysym>Enter</keysym></keycombo> flyttar "
"markeringen uppåt efter inmatningen. "
"<keycombo><keysym>Ctrl</keysym><keysym>Enter</keysym></keycombo> markerar "
"den aktuella cellen igen."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"After selecting the cell and initially entering the data, the user is in a "
"limited editing mode. The main key for editing mistakes in this mode is the "
"backspace key."
msgstr ""
"När du har markerat cellen och börjat mata in data är du i ett begränsat "
"redigeringsläge. I det läget använder du främst Backsteg för att rätta "
"misstag."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"For a more complete set of editing options, especially for longer entries, "
"there is an advanced editing mode. To enter the advanced editing mode, press"
" the <keycap>F2</keycap> function key or click on the editing region. The "
"keyboard focus will then shift from the current cell to the editing region "
"at the top of the worksheet. There, you can use cursor keys to position the "
"cursor within the data in the cell, and have all of the capabilities of the "
"data entry area available."
msgstr ""
"För fler redigeringsalternativ, särskilt vid längre inmatningar, kan du "
"använda det avancerade redigeringsläget. Tryck på funktionstangenten "
"<keycap>F2</keycap> eller klicka i redigeringsområdet för att öppna det. "
"Tangentbordsfokus flyttas då från den aktuella cellen till "
"redigeringsområdet högst upp i kalkylbladet. Där kan du använda "
"piltangenterna för att flytta markören i cellens innehåll och använda alla "
"funktioner i inmatningsfältet."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"For example, you can use: <_:variablelist-1/> See <xref linkend=\"sect-data-"
"entry\"/> For more info on the data entry area."
msgstr ""
"Du kan till exempel använda: <_:variablelist-1/> Mer information om "
"inmatningsfältet finns i <xref linkend=\"sect-data-entry\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"All the normal key bindings for GNOME application entry boxes also apply in "
"the data entry box."
msgstr ""
"Alla vanliga tangentbordsgenvägar för GNOME-programmens inmatningsfält "
"fungerar även i inmatningsfältet."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"After finishing the data entry, pressing the <keycap>Enter</keycap> key will"
" input the data entry and move the selection box downward just like for the "
"simple editing mode."
msgstr ""
"När du har matat in data trycker du på <keycap>Enter</keycap> för att "
"slutföra inmatningen och flytta markeringen nedåt, precis som i det enkla "
"redigeringsläget."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Text can be entered by selecting a cell, typing the text and then typing the"
" <keysym>Enter</keysym> key. Anything that is not interpreted to be a "
"number, boolean, formula or error will be treated as a text field. To "
"prevent <application>Gnumeric</application> from interpreting an entry as "
"one of these other elements, a leading apostrophe can be added to force the "
"entry to be text. Any entry, no matter what the contents, which starts with "
"a leading apostrophe (') will be considered to be text."
msgstr ""
"Markera en cell, skriv texten och tryck på <keysym>Enter</keysym> för att "
"mata in text. Allt som inte tolkas som ett tal, ett booleskt värde, en "
"formel eller ett fel behandlas som text. Om du vill hindra "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> från att tolka inmatningen som någon av "
"dessa andra typer kan du inleda den med en apostrof. All inmatning som "
"börjar med apostrof (') betraktas som text, oavsett innehåll."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Postal codes in the United States are series of five integers. By default, "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> interprets these to be numbers. This "
"interpretation means that the leading zeros used in the postal codes of the "
"northeastern region will be lost by default. To retain these leading zeros, "
"either the code should be entered with a leading apostrophe (e.g. '02917) or"
" the cells should be formatted as text before data entry (see <xref "
"linkend=\"sect-data-format\"/> for an explanation of formatting)."
msgstr ""
"Postnummer i USA består av fem siffror. Som standard tolkar "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> dem som tal, vilket gör att inledande "
"nollor, som används i nordöstra USA, försvinner. Behåll nollorna genom att "
"inleda koden med en apostrof (till exempel '02917) eller formatera cellerna "
"som text innan du matar in data. Se <xref linkend=\"sect-data-format\"/> om "
"cellformatering."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Numbers can be entered like other items. First the cell in which the number "
"should be entered must be selected, then a valid number must be typed in and"
" finally the entry must be inserted using the <keysym>Enter</keysym> key. "
"The valid formats for numbers are presented in <xref linkend=\"sect-data-"
"numbers\"/>."
msgstr ""
"Tal matas in på samma sätt som andra värden. Markera först cellen, skriv ett"
" giltigt tal och tryck sedan på <keysym>Enter</keysym>. Giltiga talformat "
"beskrivs i <xref linkend=\"sect-data-numbers\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"A boolean can be entered by selecting the cell, typing the boolean (either "
"TRUE or FALSE) and then typing the <keysym>Enter</keysym> key."
msgstr ""
"Mata in ett booleskt värde genom att markera cellen, skriva TRUE eller FALSE"
" och trycka på <keysym>Enter</keysym>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Formulas can be entered simply by typing a syntactically correct formula in "
"a cell. The correct syntax for formulas is explained in detail in <xref "
"linkend=\"sect-data-formulas\"/>. Formulas begin with an equals sign (=) and"
" contain arithmetic symbols, functions with their arguments and cell "
"references."
msgstr ""
"Formler matas in genom att skriva en formel med korrekt syntax i en cell. "
"Syntaxen förklaras närmare i <xref linkend=\"sect-data-formulas\"/>. Formler"
" börjar med likhetstecknet (=) och kan innehålla räknesymboler, funktioner "
"med argument och cellreferenser."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"To enter a formula, first the cell must be selected, then the correct "
"formula must be typed, and finally the <keysym>Enter</keysym> key must be "
"typed."
msgstr ""
"Markera först cellen där formeln ska stå, skriv formeln korrekt och tryck "
"sedan på <keysym>Enter</keysym>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"If the formula entered into <application>Gnumeric</application> cannot be "
"interpreted correctly, <application>Gnumeric</application> will display an "
"error message giving the user the choice of re-editing the formula or saving"
" the formula as a text field to be edited later. For example, a formula may "
"be mathematically incorrect if the user has two operators in a row (e.g. "
"=3+*4). If the formula is saved as text, when the formula is corrected the "
"leading apostrophe must be removed. <application>Gnumeric</application> will"
" then re-interpret the entry as a formula."
msgstr ""
"Om <application>Gnumeric</application> inte kan tolka en inmatad formel "
"korrekt visar <application>Gnumeric</application> ett felmeddelande med "
"möjlighet att redigera formeln igen eller spara den som text för senare "
"redigering. Formeln kan till exempel vara matematiskt felaktig om två "
"operatorer står efter varandra (till exempel =3+*4). Om formeln sparas som "
"text måste den inledande apostrofen tas bort när den har rättats. Då tolkar "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> inmatningen som en formel igen."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Formulas often include cell references or references to ranges of cells as "
"arguments to functions. These references and ranges can be entered into a "
"formula simply by typing in the proper syntax (see <xref linkend=\"sect-"
"data-formulas-references\"/> for more details). But manually entering in "
"cell ranges is slow and cumbersome. In order to speed up the entry of these "
"cell ranges, the mouse and the keyboard arrow keys can be used to select "
"these cell ranges quickly."
msgstr ""
"Formler innehåller ofta cellreferenser eller cellområden som "
"funktionsargument. Du kan skriva in referenser och områden direkt i formeln "
"med rätt syntax; se <xref linkend=\"sect-data-formulas-references\"/>. Det "
"kan dock vara långsamt och omständligt att skriva in cellområden för hand. "
"Använd musen eller piltangenterna för att välja områden snabbare."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"This version of <application>Gnumeric</application> includes 470 sheet "
"functions including all of the functions from the North American edition of "
"Microsoft Excel 2000 (TM). This version also includes numerous new functions"
" and statistical routines imported from the <application><ulink "
"type=\"http\" url=\"http://www.r-project.org/\">R</ulink></application> "
"statistical language, from the <ulink type=\"http\" "
"url=\"http://www.gnu.org/software/gsl/\">GNU Scientific Library</ulink>, and"
" from other sources. The random number generation has been updated to "
"include Beta, Cauchy, Chi-Squared, Exponential power F, Gamma, Geometric, "
"Laplace, Levy alpha-Stable Logarithmic, Logistic, Log-normal, Pareto, "
"Rayleigh Rayleigh tail, T, Type I Gumbel, Type II Gumbel, Weibull Gaussian "
"Tail, Landau, and Uniform integer distributions. The derivative valuation "
"routines have been expanded to include Black-Scholes (and sensitivities), "
"Garman Kohlhagen, Merton Jump Diffusion process, Bjerksund and Stensland "
"(American options), Forward Starts, Simple and Complex Choosers, Exchange "
"Options, options on future spreads, and most favourable state payouts. The "
"solver has been improved with new linear and quadratic programming routines."
" There were improvements in the T-Test, Z-Test, and F-Test. More accuracy "
"for GEOMDIST, BINOMDIST, BETADIST, BETAINV, FINV, CAUCHY, FDIST, FTEST, "
"HYPGEOMDIST, ERF, FISHER, EFFECT, NOMINAL, MIRR, IRR, XNPV, NPV, PMT, RATE, "
"PV, FV, IPMT, PPMT, ZTEST, EXPM1, LN1P."
msgstr ""
"Den här versionen av <application>Gnumeric</application> innehåller 470 "
"kalkylbladsfunktioner, däribland alla funktioner från den nordamerikanska "
"utgåvan av Microsoft Excel 2000 (TM). Versionen innehåller också många nya "
"funktioner och statistiska rutiner från statistikprogramspråket "
"<application><ulink type=\"http\" "
"url=\"http://www.r-project.org/\">R</ulink></application>, <ulink "
"type=\"http\" url=\"http://www.gnu.org/software/gsl/\">GNU Scientific "
"Library</ulink> och andra källor. Slumptalsgeneratorn har utökats med "
"fördelningarna beta, Cauchy, chi-två, exponential, power F, gamma, "
"geometrisk, Laplace, Lévy alfa-stabil, logaritmisk, logistisk, lognormal, "
"Pareto, Rayleigh och Rayleigh-svans, t, Gumbel typ I och II, Weibull, "
"Gaussisk svans, Landau samt diskret likformig. Rutinerna för värdering av "
"derivat har utökats med Black-Scholes (och dess känslighetsmått), Garman-"
"Kohlhagen, Mertons hoppdiffusionsprocess, Bjerksund och Stensland "
"(amerikanska optioner), optioner med framtida start, enkla och komplexa "
"chooser-optioner, bytesoptioner, optioner på spreadar med terminskontrakt "
"samt utbetalningar i mest gynnsamma tillstånd. Lösaren har förbättrats med "
"nya linjära och kvadratiska optimeringsrutiner. T-testet, Z-testet och "
"F-testet har förbättrats. Beräkningarna har blivit noggrannare för GEOMDIST,"
" BINOMDIST, BETADIST, BETAINV, FINV, CAUCHY, FDIST, FTEST, HYPGEOMDIST, ERF,"
" FISHER, EFFECT, NOMINAL, MIRR, IRR, XNPV, NPV, PMT, RATE, PV, FV, IPMT, "
"PPMT, ZTEST, EXPM1 och LN1P."

