#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "Bar Plots"
msgstr "Stapeldiagram"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Bar plots present the numeric values of categorical data with the data "
"values of each series represented as a horizontal bar. Sequential data "
"values are considered to belong to different categories and are plotted "
"along the vertical axis at equally spaced intervals. The data values from "
"different series are assigned to these categories based on the position of "
"the value in the series, for example, the second data value taken from each "
"series all share one category. The data values are plotted along the "
"horizontal (X) axis as bars of different lengths and positions depending on "
"the numeric content of the data value and the particular sub-type chosen for"
" the bar plot."
msgstr ""
"Stapeldiagram visar numeriska värden för kategoridata som horisontella "
"staplar, en per värde i varje serie. Värden i följd hör till olika "
"kategorier och placeras med jämna mellanrum längs den vertikala axeln. "
"Värden från olika serier kopplas till kategorier utifrån sin position i "
"serien; det andra värdet i varje serie hör till exempel till samma kategori."
" Värdena visas som staplar längs den horisontella (X-)axeln. Staplarnas "
"längd och placering beror på värdet och den valda undertypen."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Bar plot sub-types provide three options for relating the values from "
"different data series. The first sub-type plots each series independently in"
" adjacent bars, each of which is tied to the vertical axis and has its "
"length determined by the numeric content of the data value. The second sub-"
"type plots each series as a horizontally stacked set of bars with the "
"horizontal length of each element determined by the numeric content of the "
"data value and the position of the bar determined by the position of the "
"element in the data series. For example, if the first series starts with "
"values <literal>{3.9, 4.2, ...}</literal>, the second series with values "
"<literal>{1.2, 3.5, ...}</literal>, and the third series with values "
"<literal>{3.1, 1.9, ...}</literal>, then the third bar will be plotted "
"ranging from 7.7 to 9.6, since <literal>7.7=4.2+3.5</literal> and "
"<literal>9.6=4.2+3.5+1.9</literal>. The third sub-type plots each series as "
"a horizontally stacked set of bars scaled to the total all the numeric "
"values in that category. Using the example above, the three bars would range"
" from 0 to 0.4375, from 0.4375 to 0.8020, and from 0.8020 to 1 respectively "
"because the intervals are the proportional contribution of each data value "
"to the total, i.e. <literal>0.4375=4.2/(4.2+3.5+1.9)</literal> for the "
"first, <literal>0.3645...=3.5/(4.2+3.5+1.9)</literal> for the second, and "
"<literal>0.1979...=1.9/(4.2+3.5+1.9)</literal> for the third. By default, "
"these numbers are presented as percentages on the horizontal (X) axis."
msgstr ""
"Undertyperna anger hur värden från olika dataserier förhåller sig till "
"varandra. Den första visar varje serie separat i staplar bredvid varandra. "
"Varje stapel utgår från den vertikala axeln och får sin längd av datavärdet."
" Den andra visar serierna som horisontellt staplade staplar. Varje dels "
"längd bestäms av datavärdet, och stapelns läge av dess position i serien. Om"
" den första serien till exempel börjar med värdena <literal>{3.9, 4.2, "
"...}</literal>, den andra med <literal>{1.2, 3.5, ...}</literal> och den "
"tredje med <literal>{3.1, 1.9, ...}</literal>, sträcker sig den tredje "
"stapeln från 7.7 till 9.6, eftersom <literal>7.7=4.2+3.5</literal> och "
"<literal>9.6=4.2+3.5+1.9</literal>. Den tredje undertypen visar serierna som"
" horisontellt staplade staplar, skalade efter summan av alla värden i "
"kategorin. Med exemplet ovan sträcker sig staplarna från 0 till 0.4375, från"
" 0.4375 till 0.8020 och från 0.8020 till 1. Intervallen motsvarar varje "
"datavärdes andel av summan: <literal>0.4375=4.2/(4.2+3.5+1.9)</literal> för "
"den första, <literal>0.3645...=3.5/(4.2+3.5+1.9)</literal> för den andra och"
" <literal>0.1979...=1.9/(4.2+3.5+1.9)</literal> för den tredje. Som standard"
" visas värdena som procentsatser på den horisontella (X-)axeln."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "Bar plots do not have any pre-defined styles."
msgstr "Stapeldiagram har inga fördefinierade stilar."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "An example of bar plots"
msgstr "Exempel på stapeldiagram"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"A screenshot of a table of data and three bar plots made using those data."
msgstr ""
"Skärmbild av en datatabell och tre stapeldiagram som bygger på tabellens "
"värden."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"This screenshot shows a table of data and three bar plots. The data consist "
"of three series organized by row and starting with the words \"Widgets\", "
"\"Gadgets\", and \"Lumpets\". Each of these series has values in five "
"categories. The three graphs illustrate the three sub-types of bar plots, "
"with the series plotted independently in the left plot, stacked in the "
"middle plot, and proportionately stacked in the right plot."
msgstr ""
"Skärmbilden visar en datatabell och tre stapeldiagram. Data består av tre "
"radorienterade serier som börjar med etiketterna ”Widgets”, ”Gadgets” och "
"”Lumpets”. Varje serie innehåller värden för fem kategorier. Diagrammen "
"visar de tre undertyperna: serierna visas var för sig till vänster, staplade"
" i mitten och proportionellt staplade till höger."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Each series in bar plots can include three main elements and two error "
"elements, although only the value element is necessary. The series can have "
"a 'Name' element, which is a single text entry used to identify the series, "
"must have a 'Values' element, which is a sequence of numeric values, and may"
" have a 'Label' element, which is a sequence of text entries used to "
"identify the categories. All of these elements can be defined as references "
"to a region of the worksheet, as literally defined entries, or as formula "
"expressions which result in the correct type. The 'Label' element is shared "
"by all of the series. The legend added to a bar plot identifies the "
"different series, by default using the entries of the 'Name' element of each"
" series. The two error elements include a list for errors in the positive "
"direction and one for errors in the negative direction."
msgstr ""
"Varje dataserie i ett stapeldiagram kan innehålla tre huvudkomponenter och "
"två felkomponenter, men bara värdekomponenten är nödvändig. Serien kan ha "
"komponenten ”Namn”, ett textvärde som identifierar serien. Den måste ha "
"komponenten ”Värden”, en följd av numeriska värden, och kan även ha "
"komponenten ”Etikett”, en följd av textvärden som identifierar kategorierna."
" Komponenterna kan anges som referenser till ett område i kalkylbladet, som "
"fasta värden eller som formeluttryck som ger rätt datatyp. Alla serier delar"
" på komponenten ”Etikett”. Förklaringen till stapeldiagrammet identifierar "
"serierna och använder som standard värdena i respektive series komponent "
"”Namn”. De två felkomponenterna innehåller listor med positiva respektive "
"negativa felvärden."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "The data in each bar plot series"
msgstr "Data i varje dataserie i ett stapeldiagram"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"A single textual element labeling the data series. These will be used in the"
" legend which may be displayed with the bar plot."
msgstr ""
"Ett textvärde som namnger dataserien. Det kan visas i stapeldiagrammets "
"förklaring."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"A series of textual elements labeling each value. Generally, this series "
"will have as many entries as there were in the \"Value\" series. These "
"entries are shared by all the series in the bar plot."
msgstr ""
"En följd av textvärden som etiketterar varje värde. Följden innehåller "
"vanligen lika många poster som serien ”Värden”. Alla serier i "
"stapeldiagrammet delar på dessa etiketter."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Bar plots provide three icons to choose one of the three bar plot sub-types."
msgstr "Tre ikoner motsvarar de tre undertyperna av stapeldiagram."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "Bar plot sub-type and style options."
msgstr "Alternativ för undertyp och stil i stapeldiagram."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/chart_bar_1_1.png\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>"
" The icon for a bar plot of the sub-type with independent, adjacent bars. "
"</phrase> </textobject> </inlinemediaobject>"
msgstr ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/chart_bar_1_1.png\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>"
" Ikon för undertypen med fristående staplar bredvid varandra. </phrase> "
"</textobject> </inlinemediaobject>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The icon for a bar plot of the sub-type with independent, adjacent bars."
msgstr "Ikon för undertypen med fristående staplar bredvid varandra."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/chart_bar_1_2.png\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>"
" The icon for a bar plot of the sub-type with horizontally stacked bars. "
"</phrase> </textobject> </inlinemediaobject>"
msgstr ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/chart_bar_1_2.png\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>"
" Ikon för undertypen med horisontellt staplade staplar. </phrase> "
"</textobject> </inlinemediaobject>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The icon for a bar plot of the sub-type with horizontally stacked bars."
msgstr "Ikon för undertypen med horisontellt staplade staplar."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/chart_bar_1_3.png\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>"
" The icon for a bar plot of the sub-type with horizontally stacked, "
"proportionately scaled bars. </phrase> </textobject> </inlinemediaobject>"
msgstr ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/chart_bar_1_3.png\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>"
" Ikon för undertypen med horisontellt staplade, proportionellt skalade "
"staplar. </phrase> </textobject> </inlinemediaobject>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The icon for a bar plot of the sub-type with horizontally stacked, "
"proportionately scaled bars."
msgstr ""
"Ikon för undertypen med horisontellt staplade, proportionellt skalade "
"staplar."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "Pie Plots"
msgstr "Cirkeldiagram"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Pie plots present the numeric values from a single series of categorical "
"data as slices of a circular area, the angular arc of each slice determined "
"by the proportional magnitude of each value compared to the overall sum of "
"all the values. For example, if the series had values { 1.12, 4.48, 3.36, "
"1.68, 0.56}, the contribution of each slice to the total would be {0.10, "
"0.40, 0.330, 0.15, 0.0 5}, since <literal>0.10= "
"1.12/(1.12+4.48+3.36+1.68+0.56)</literal>, and the angular arcs of the "
"wedges would be {36, 144, 108, 54, 18} degrees, since "
"<literal>36=0.10*360</literal>."
msgstr ""
"Cirkeldiagram visar de numeriska värdena i en enda dataserie som sektorer i "
"en cirkel. Varje sektors vinkel motsvarar dess värde som andel av summan av "
"alla värden. Om serien till exempel innehåller värdena { 1.12, 4.48, 3.36, "
"1.68, 0.56}, blir sektorernas andelar av summan {0.10, 0.40, 0.330, 0.15, "
"0.0 5}, eftersom <literal>0.10= 1.12/(1.12+4.48+3.36+1.68+0.56)</literal>. "
"Sektorernas vinklar blir då {36, 144, 108, 54, 18} grader, eftersom "
"<literal>36=0.10*360</literal>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "Pie plots do not have any sub-types."
msgstr "Cirkeldiagram har inga undertyper."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Pie plot styles provide two choices for the rendering of the pie chart, "
"either with all slices linked into one overall circle, or with gaps between "
"the slices. The size of the gap is a property of the pie plot which can be "
"changed."
msgstr ""
"Cirkeldiagram har två stilar: sektorerna kan bilda en sammanhängande cirkel "
"eller skiljas åt av mellanrum. Mellanrummets storlek kan ändras i "
"diagrammets egenskaper."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "An example of a pie plot"
msgstr "Exempel på cirkeldiagram"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"A screenshot of a worksheet area showing a data table and a pie plot made "
"with those data."
msgstr ""
"Skärmbild av ett kalkylblad med en datatabell och ett cirkeldiagram som "
"bygger på värdena."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"This screenshot shows a table of data and a pie plot. The data consist of a "
"single data series organized in a row and starting with the word "
"\"Widgets\". The series has values in five categories. The legend includes "
"the names of the different data categories."
msgstr ""
"Skärmbilden visar en datatabell och ett cirkeldiagram. Data består av en "
"dataserie i en rad som börjar med ordet ”Widgets”. Serien innehåller värden "
"för fem kategorier. Förklaringen visar kategoriernas namn."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Each pie plot contains a single series which can include three elements "
"although only the value element is necessary. The series can have a 'Name' "
"element, which is a single text entry used to identify the series, must have"
" a 'Values' element, which is a sequence of numeric values, and may have a "
"'Label' element, which is a sequence of text entries used to identify the "
"categories. All of these elements can be defined as references to a region "
"of the worksheet, as literally defined entries, or as formula expressions "
"which result in the correct type. The legend added to a pie plot identifies "
"the different categories using the entries in the 'Label' element."
msgstr ""
"Varje cirkeldiagram innehåller en enda serie, som kan ha tre komponenter men"
" måste ha en värdekomponent. Serien kan ha komponenten ”Namn”, ett textvärde"
" som identifierar serien. Den måste ha komponenten ”Värden”, en följd av "
"numeriska värden, och kan även ha komponenten ”Etikett”, en följd av "
"textvärden som identifierar kategorierna. Komponenterna kan anges som "
"referenser till ett cellområde i kalkylbladet, som fasta värden eller som "
"formeluttryck som ger rätt datatyp. Förklaringen i cirkeldiagrammet visar "
"kategoriernas namn från komponenten ”Etikett”."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "The data in each pie plot series"
msgstr "Data i varje serie i ett cirkeldiagram"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"A list of textual entries labeling the category of each value. Generally, "
"this series will have as many entries as there were in the 'Value' list. "
"These will be used in the legend which may be displayed with the pie plot."
msgstr ""
"En lista med textetiketter för varje värdes kategori. Listan innehåller "
"vanligen lika många poster som listan ”Värden”. Etiketterna kan visas i "
"cirkeldiagrammets förklaring."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Pie plots do not have any sub-types but provide two icons to distinguish the"
" style of the plot allowing a choice between pie plots which comprise a "
"single circular area or plots with distinct pie slices separated by small "
"gaps."
msgstr ""
"Cirkeldiagram har inga undertyper, men två ikoner skiljer stilarna åt: en "
"sammanhängande cirkel eller sektorer med små mellanrum."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/chart_pie_1_1.png\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>"
" The icon for a pie plot of the style with joint slices. </phrase> "
"</textobject> </inlinemediaobject>"
msgstr ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/chart_pie_1_1.png\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>"
" Ikon för cirkeldiagram med sammanhängande sektorer. </phrase> </textobject>"
" </inlinemediaobject>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "The icon for a pie plot of the style with joint slices."
msgstr "Ikon för cirkeldiagram med sammanhängande sektorer."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/chart_pie_2_1.png\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>"
" The icon for a pie plot of the style with separated slices. </phrase> "
"</textobject> </inlinemediaobject>"
msgstr ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/chart_pie_2_1.png\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>"
" Ikon för cirkeldiagram med åtskilda sektorer. </phrase> </textobject> "
"</inlinemediaobject>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "The icon for a pie plot of the style with separated slices."
msgstr "Ikon för cirkeldiagram med åtskilda sektorer."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "Ring Plots"
msgstr "Ringdiagram"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Ring plots present the numeric values of categorical data as segments of "
"circular rings. Sequential data values are considered to belong to different"
" categories and are plotted with distinct patterns. The data values from "
"different series are assigned to these categories based on the position of "
"the value in the series, for example, the second data value taken from each "
"series all share one category. The data values are used to determine the "
"size of the arc based on the proportionate size of the data value to the sum"
" of all data values in the series. For example, if the series had values { "
"1.12, 4.48, 3.36, 1.68, 0.56}, the contribution of each ring section to the "
"total would be {0.10, 0.40, 0.330, 0.15, 0.0 5}, since <literal>0.10= "
"1.12/(1.12+4.48+3.36+1.68+0.56)</literal>, and the angular arcs of the "
"sections would be {36, 144, 108, 54, 18} degrees, since "
"<literal>36=0.10*360</literal>."
msgstr ""
"Ringdiagram visar numeriska kategorivärden som segment i koncentriska "
"ringar. Värden i följd hör till olika kategorier och visas med olika "
"mönster. Värden från olika serier kopplas till kategorier utifrån sin "
"position i serien; det andra värdet i varje serie hör till exempel till "
"samma kategori. Segmentens vinkel bestäms av respektive värdes andel av "
"summan i serien. Om serien till exempel innehåller värdena { 1.12, 4.48, "
"3.36, 1.68, 0.56}, blir segmentens andelar av summan {0.10, 0.40, 0.330, "
"0.15, 0.0 5}, eftersom <literal>0.10= "
"1.12/(1.12+4.48+3.36+1.68+0.56)</literal>. Segmentens vinklar blir då {36, "
"144, 108, 54, 18} grader, eftersom <literal>36=0.10*360</literal>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "Ring plots do not have any sub-types."
msgstr "Ringdiagram har inga undertyper."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Ring plot styles provide two choices. Ring plots can be plotted with all "
"segments linked into a single overall ring, with different series plotted "
"immediately adjacent to one another in sequentially larger rings. "
"Alternatively, the segments of the outermost ring can be split and float a "
"certain distance away from the next ring."
msgstr ""
"Ringdiagram har två stilar. Alla segment kan bilda en sammanhängande ring, "
"där serierna visas i intilliggande ringar med ökande storlek. Alternativt "
"kan segmenten i den yttersta ringen delas upp och skiljas från nästa ring."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "An example of ring plots"
msgstr "Exempel på ringdiagram"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"A screenshot of a worksheet area showing a data table and two ring plots "
"made with those data."
msgstr ""
"Skärmbild av ett kalkylblad med en datatabell och två ringdiagram som bygger"
" på värdena."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"This screenshot shows a table of data and two ring plots. The data consist "
"of a single data series organized in a row and starting with the word "
"\"Widgets\". The data consist of three series organized by row and starting "
"with the words \"Widgets\", \"Gadgets\", and \"Lumpets\". Each of these "
"series has values in five categories. The two graphs illustrate the two sub-"
"types of ring plots, the left most plot without any gaps and the right most "
"plot having the outer plot with gaps."
msgstr ""
"Skärmbilden visar en datatabell och två ringdiagram. Data består av en enda "
"dataserie i en rad som börjar med ordet ”Widgets”. Data består av tre "
"radorienterade serier som börjar med etiketterna ”Widgets”, ”Gadgets” och "
"”Lumpets”. Varje serie innehåller värden för fem kategorier. Diagrammen "
"visar de två undertyperna: det vänstra saknar mellanrum och det högra har "
"mellanrum i den yttersta ringen."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Each series in ring plots can include three main elements and two error "
"elements, although only the value element is necessary. The series can have "
"a 'Name' element, which is a single text entry used to identify the series, "
"must have a 'Values' element, which is a sequence of numeric values, and may"
" have a 'Label' element, which is a sequence of text entries used to "
"identify the categories. All of these elements can be defined as references "
"to a region of the worksheet, as literally defined entries, or as formula "
"expressions which result in the correct type. The 'Label' element is shared "
"by all of the series. The legend added to a ring plot identifies the "
"different series, by default using the entries of the 'Name' element of each"
" series. The two error elements include a list for errors in the positive "
"direction and one for errors in the negative direction."
msgstr ""
"Varje dataserie i ett ringdiagram kan innehålla tre huvudkomponenter och två"
" felkomponenter, men bara värdekomponenten är nödvändig. Serien kan ha "
"komponenten ”Namn”, ett textvärde som identifierar serien. Den måste ha "
"komponenten ”Värden”, en följd av numeriska värden, och kan även ha "
"komponenten ”Etikett”, en följd av textvärden som identifierar kategorierna."
" Komponenterna kan anges som referenser till ett cellområde i kalkylbladet, "
"som fasta värden eller som formeluttryck som ger rätt datatyp. Alla serier "
"delar på komponenten ”Etikett”. Förklaringen i ringdiagrammet identifierar "
"serierna och använder som standard värdena i respektive series komponent "
"”Namn”. De två felkomponenterna innehåller listor med positiva respektive "
"negativa felvärden."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "The data in each ring plot series"
msgstr "Data i varje serie i ett ringdiagram"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "Ring plots provide two icons distinguishing the two different styles."
msgstr "Två ikoner skiljer stilarna för ringdiagram åt."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "Ring plot sub-type and style options."
msgstr "Alternativ för undertyp och stil i ringdiagram."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/chart_ring_1_1.png\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> "
"<phrase> The icon for a ring plot with the style of displaying series in "
"contiguous rings. </phrase> </textobject> </inlinemediaobject>"
msgstr ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/chart_ring_1_1.png\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> "
"<phrase> Ikon för ringdiagram med serier i sammanhängande ringar. </phrase> "
"</textobject> </inlinemediaobject>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The icon for a ring plot with the style of displaying series in contiguous "
"rings."
msgstr "Ikon för ringdiagram med serier i sammanhängande ringar."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/chart_ring_1_2.png\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> "
"<phrase> The icon for a ring plot with the style of displaying the outermost"
" series separated from the rest. </phrase> </textobject> "
"</inlinemediaobject>"
msgstr ""
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"figures/chart_ring_1_2.png\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> "
"<phrase> Ikon för ringdiagram där den yttersta serien skiljs från de övriga."
" </phrase> </textobject> </inlinemediaobject>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The icon for a ring plot with the style of displaying the outermost series "
"separated from the rest."
msgstr "Ikon för ringdiagram där den yttersta serien skiljs från de övriga."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "Pie plots"
msgstr "Cirkeldiagram"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Pie plots represent the data values as slices of a circular area, with the "
"central angle of each slice, or wedge, proportional to the size of the value"
" compared to the sum of all the values in the series."
msgstr ""
"Cirkeldiagram visar datavärden som sektorer i en cirkel. Varje sektors "
"medelpunktsvinkel står i proportion till värdets storlek jämfört med summan "
"av alla värden i serien."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "The configurable properties of a pie plot."
msgstr "Egenskaper som kan ställas in för cirkeldiagram."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"This screenshot depicts the properties of a pie plot which can be "
"configured."
msgstr ""
"Skärmbilden visar egenskaperna för ett cirkeldiagram som kan ställas in."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Pie plots can be displayed with the slices separated from each other which "
"in certain situations may improve the visual clarity of a pie plot. The "
"second spin button allows the slices to be separated."
msgstr ""
"Sektorerna i ett cirkeldiagram kan visas åtskilda, vilket ibland gör "
"diagrammet tydligare. Den andra stegningsrutan används för att ange "
"avståndet mellan sektorerna."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The colors of each slice, by default, are all different to allow the easy "
"visual distinction between each slice. Since pie plots only allow a single "
"series to be plotted, there is no need to use color to associate the values "
"from different series. By unchecking this box, all of the slices in a pie "
"chart can be made to follow the color scheme defined in the plot series "
"<guilabel>Style</guilabel> tab. However, if this box is unchecked, the "
"outlines of the slices must be styled with a different color for the slices "
"to be distinguishable."
msgstr ""
"Som standard har sektorerna olika färger så att de lätt kan skiljas åt. "
"Eftersom ett cirkeldiagram bara visar en serie behöver färgerna inte "
"användas för att skilja olika serier åt. Om du avmarkerar rutan får "
"sektorerna i cirkeldiagrammet färgschemat från diagramseriens flik "
"<guilabel>Stil</guilabel>. Då måste sektorernas konturer ha olika färger för"
" att de ska gå att skilja åt."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "Ring plots"
msgstr "Ringdiagram"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Ring plots are similar to pie plots but may have an empty center and can be "
"made with multiple series."
msgstr ""
"Ringdiagram liknar cirkeldiagram, men kan ha ett tomt centrum och innehålla "
"flera dataserier."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "The configurable properties of a ring plot."
msgstr "Egenskaper som kan ställas in för ringdiagram."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"This screenshot depicts the properties of a ring plot which can be "
"configured."
msgstr ""
"Skärmbilden visar egenskaperna för ett ringdiagram som kan ställas in."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Like pie plots, ring plots assign values to the slices of a circular area by"
" representing the magnitude of the value by the central angle of the slice, "
"although for ring plots the center of the circular area is empty. Like pie "
"plots, the first slice is plotted starting clockwise from the vertical and "
"this first option can change the beginning point of the first slice's angle."
msgstr ""
"Precis som i cirkeldiagram visas värden i ringdiagram som sektorer vars "
"medelpunktsvinkel motsvarar värdets storlek. Ringdiagram har dock ett tomt "
"centrum. Den första sektorn börjar lodrätt uppåt och fortsätter medurs, "
"precis som i ett cirkeldiagram. Den första inställningen ändrar sektorns "
"startvinkel."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"The slices of a ring plot can also be separated. The <guilabel>Slice "
"Separation</guilabel> option allows a user to determine the proportional "
"size of the gap between slices."
msgstr ""
"Sektorerna i ett ringdiagram kan också skiljas åt. Med alternativet "
"<guilabel>Avstånd mellan sektorer</guilabel> anger du mellanrummets storlek "
"i förhållande till sektorerna."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Certain plot types require accessory components such as the elements related"
" to the creation of a Cartesian coordinate system. Charts which include one "
"or more plots of this kind will have a Grid and may have X (horizontal) and "
"Y (vertical) axes."
msgstr ""
"Vissa diagramtyper behöver hjälpelement för att skapa ett kartesiskt "
"koordinatsystem. Diagram med en eller flera sådana typer har ett rutnät och "
"kan även ha X-axel (vågrät) och Y-axel (lodrät)."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Axes are used in several different kinds of plots to provide quantitative "
"indexes for the scale of each plot direction. "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> uses four different kinds of axes. "
"<guilabel>Category</guilabel> axes do not provide a quantitative scale but "
"merely distinguish each different category by providing space for the values"
" of the category along the axis. <guilabel>Continuous</guilabel> axes "
"provide a quantitative measure of each value based on the projection of that"
" value onto the axis. <guilabel>Radial</guilabel> axes are used in radar "
"plots and are continuous axes which radiate from a central point. "
"<guilabel>Circular</guilabel> axes have not yet been implemented."
msgstr ""
"Axlar används i flera diagramtyper för att ange skalan i varje riktning. "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> har fyra typer av axlar. "
"<guilabel>Kategori</guilabel> ger ingen kvantitativ skala utan skiljer "
"kategorierna åt och placerar deras värden längs axeln. "
"<guilabel>Kontinuerlig</guilabel> anger ett kvantitativt mått för varje "
"värde utifrån dess projektion på axeln. <guilabel>Radiell</guilabel> används"
" i radardiagram och strålar som kontinuerlig axel ut från en mittpunkt. "
"<guilabel>Cirkulär</guilabel> har ännu inte implementerats."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Line, column and area charts use a category axis to separate the categories "
"along the horizontal direction and a continuous axis to distinguish values "
"in the vertical direction. Bar charts reverse these two axes. XY scatter "
"plots and bubble plots use two continuous axes, one in the horizontal "
"direction, the X-axis, and one in the vertical direction, the Y-axis. Radar "
"plots use three or more continuous axes radiating from a central point. Pie "
"and Ring plots do not use any axes."
msgstr ""
"Linje-, kolumn- och areadiagram använder en kategori-axel för att skilja "
"kategorierna åt vågrätt och en kontinuerlig axel för värdena lodrätt. "
"Stapeldiagram använder axlarna omvänt. XY-punktdiagram och bubbeldiagram "
"använder två kontinuerliga axlar: X-axeln vågrätt och Y-axeln lodrätt. "
"Radardiagram använder minst tre kontinuerliga axlar som strålar ut från en "
"mittpunkt. Cirkeldiagram och ringdiagram använder inga axlar."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Axes have properties related to the outer bounds of the axis, the style of "
"the line drawn for the axis, the font style of the markers along the axis, "
"detail properties of the tics and other markers on the axis, and the number "
"format of the axis markers."
msgstr ""
"Axlar har egenskaper för sina gränser, axellinjens stil, teckensnittet för "
"markeringarna längs axeln, skalstreck och andra markeringar samt talformatet"
" för axelvärdena."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Axis labels share the same properties related to the style of their "
"background rectangular panel, including the fill and outline properties, "
"have properties related to the style of the font used for the text, "
"including the font type, style and size, and the data contents of the text "
"used to label the axis."
msgstr ""
"Axelns etiketter har egenskaper för den rektangulära bakgrundspanelen, bland"
" annat fyllning och kontur. De har även egenskaper för etiketternas "
"teckensnitt, däribland typ, stil och storlek, samt för textens innehåll."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"When an internal link is activated by clicking on the cell, the range of "
"cells given by the link address becomes the current selection. The cell "
"closest to A1 in the new selection becomes the active cell."
msgstr ""
"När du klickar på cellen för att aktivera en intern länk blir cellområdet "
"som anges av länkadressen den aktuella markeringen. Cellen närmast A1 i det "
"nya området blir aktiv."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "Defining Names"
msgstr "Definiera namn"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"Names are labels with a meaning defined in the spreadsheet or by "
"<application>Gnumeric</application>. Names can be defined for a whole "
"workbook or for just a single worksheet. A name can refer to a numeric "
"value, a string, a range of cells, or a formula. A name can be used wherever"
" its meaning could otherwise be used."
msgstr ""
"Namn är etiketter med en betydelse som definieras i kalkylbladet eller i "
"<application>Gnumeric</application>. Namn kan definieras för hela "
"arbetsboken eller för ett enskilt blad. Ett namn kan syfta på ett numeriskt "
"värde, en textsträng, ett cellområde eller en formel. Du kan använda namnet "
"överallt där du annars skulle använda dess värde."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"If the second column shows a minus sign, the line is for a user-defined "
"name. Click on the minus sign to delete the definition of the name. If the "
"second column shows a padlock icon, the definition is created automatically "
"and cannot be modified from this dialog."
msgstr ""
"Om den andra kolumnen visar ett minustecken gäller raden ett "
"användardefinierat namn. Klicka på minustecknet för att ta bort namnets "
"definition. Om kolumnen visar en hänglåsikon skapas definitionen automatiskt"
" och kan inte ändras i den här dialogrutan."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"For user-defined names, the third column of the <guimenu>Define "
"Names</guimenu> dialog contains a downward- or upward-pointing arrow. Click "
"on the arrow to move the definition down to the worksheet or up to the "
"workbook. This operation is not permitted if the moved definition would "
"replace a name already defined for the destination. To do such a "
"replacement, first delete the name in the destination, then move the "
"definition."
msgstr ""
"För användardefinierade namn visar den tredje kolumnen i dialogrutan "
"<guimenu>Definiera namn</guimenu> en pil som pekar uppåt eller nedåt. Klicka"
" på pilen för att flytta definitionen till bladet eller arbetsboken. Du kan "
"inte göra det om definitionen skulle ersätta ett namn som redan finns där. "
"Ta i så fall först bort namnet på målet och flytta sedan definitionen."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid ""
"In addition to the names defined by the user, "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> has some pre-defined names for useful "
"elements:"
msgstr ""
"Utöver de namn som användaren definierar har "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> några fördefinierade namn för användbara"
" element:"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "Sheet_Title: The name of the current sheet."
msgstr "Sheet_Title: Namnet på det aktuella bladet."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
msgid "In the following cells, enter the equations below in the 'Profit' tab:"
msgstr "Ange följande formler i cellerna på fliken ”Profit”:"

